nquery. If you handle `applied` yourself, do the same, or the page may evaluate its empty-search guard without the\nbasket. See the pitfalls of the collections list."],[285,"`injected` (or `provideAccessPrincipal()`, for the providers way) forces users or groups into `owners` or\n`readers`. They are in the emitted lists from the start, and no action — add, remove, change a role — can drop\nthem; picking one in the search adds nothing twice. `mode` decides how they look:"],[2749,"`injectFloatingPanel()` positions a panel against an anchor with Floating UI. It is what `Select`, `Autocomplete`,\n`SubMenu` and a combobox's popup in general need, and what each of them used to write by hand: wait for the panel and the\nanchor, follow them with `autoUpdate`, compute the position, write `left` and `top`, stop on destroy. For a panel opened by\na button and light-dismissed, `PopoverDirective` is enough; reach for this one when the anchor is not the\ntrigger, the panel is created later (a combobox renders its popup when it opens), or it must not close on an outside press."],[2039,"`injectWorkspaceMention()` gives the same state with no markup. Call it from a component's field initializer."],[1268,"`InlineWorker` — running a function in a Web Worker"],[2246,"`InputGroup` wraps a native `<input>` in a styled flex container — no JavaScript state duplication, every\nvisual state (focus, disabled, read-only) is driven by CSS `has-[]` selectors reading the native control's own\nstate."],[2992,"`inset` and `floating` variants"],[2684,"`isTouch()` and `provideInputModality()`: how the library tells a finger from a mouse."],[2583,"`isTouch` is the answer to \"can the user hover?\": an iPad in landscape is wider than 768px, so `isMobile()` is `false`\nthere, yet nothing hovers. Use it for hover-only actions, for the size of a target and for keyboard hints."],[2787,"`itemSelected` bound only on the root `<Menu>` still fires for an item selected several `SubMenu` levels deep —\nselection