ivate** (visible only to the user who added it). `<multiselect-labels>` is the field that adds and removes\nthem on one article field; `EditLabels` is the dialog that shows the public and private fields together for a\nsingle document."],[1709,"A **switch**, saved as soon as it is flipped, written as a real boolean (never the string `\"true\"`)."],[41,"A **token** is a CSS custom property published by the design system — `--bg-primary-base`,\n`--font-primary-muted`, `--row-height-xs` — rather than a raw Tailwind utility or a literal colour. Every\n`galactik` component is styled exclusively through these tokens, so an application that declares them gets a\nconsistent look with zero component-level configuration."],[1981,"A *workspace* is a named set of documents that a user creates, fills by uploading files, shares with other\npeople and previews. It is backed by the Agent Workspace API of `@sinequa/atomic` (`api/v2/agent-workspace/*`)."],[658,"A `category` axis, never `\"time\"` — this library ships no Chart.js date adapter, and setting\n`scales.x.type = \"time\"` without one compiles perfectly and throws at runtime. Bucket labels are resolved by\n`buildTimeline()` (a pure function, unit-testable without a chart), which also fills gaps: an empty bucket is\ndrawn flat at zero rather than skipped, so the shape of the series is never silently misrepresented."],[2391,"A `height` utility on the control cancels `field-sizing` outright. Bound the height with `minRows`/`maxRows` on\nthe wrapper instead of a fixed `h-*` class on the control in `auto` mode."],[2486,"A `ListItemAction` is **not focusable**: its host `ListItem` is a listbox `option`, and ARIA forbids an option from\ncontaining an interactive control. A mouse user clicks the icon, which appears on hover. A keyboard user presses\nthe action's key while the row has focus, and `ListItem` calls the action's `trigger()` — your `(click)` handler\nfires exactly as it would for a click."],[695,"A bar, pie or doughnut chart, from the Chart.js entry point."],[1368,"A bare `@if` around projected content does not carry the `slot` attribute the content projection matches on —\nwrap it in an `<ng-container slot=\"extra-actions\">` (as in the recipe above), not a bare `@if` directly around\nthe action."],[505,"A basket is the backend's name for a collection: a named list of document ids, stored per user. `Basket` (from\n`@sinequa/atomic-angular`'s models) is `{ name: string; ids?: string[] }` — the type every component on this\npage reads and writes."],[164,"A bookmark remembers one document; a **saved search** remembers a whole search state — the query text, every\napplied filter, the sort order — as the URL that reproduces it. `<saved-search-popover>` is the starred toggle\nthat saves or unsaves the *current* search in one click; `<saved-searches>` is the paginated list of everything\nthe user has saved."],[2654,"A browser that does not start a native drag on touch leaves no way to reorder: the keyboard shortcut is the only\nalternative, and it is not available there either. Offer another control (move up and down buttons) where touch\nmatters."],[2436,"A bullet has no text, so on its own it says nothing to assistive technology — when the label next to it\nalready names the status, that is correct: the dot is decoration, and stays out of the accessibility tree. Set\n`aria-label` only when the dot is the *only* indication of the state, and it renders `role=\"img\"` with that\naccessible name."],[2715,"A callable dialog is mounted in `document.body`. That is a problem when the caller lives in a native\n`popover=\"auto\"` (the `[popover]` directive, a filter panel, a dropdown): `showModal()` hides every auto popover\nthat is **not an ancestor of the dialog**, so the popover closes the instant the dialog opens — and whatever\nthe popover rendered is destroyed with it, the dialog included."],[2736,"A callable dialog outlives the component that opened it: if that component is destroyed while the dialog is\nopen, the promise stays pending, and whatever eventually ends the call resumes your code on a component that no\nlonger exists."],[867,"A chip's identity is its **leaf filter**, not its value: a date distribution's two bounds can share one value\n(\"This year\" is `modified >= 2026-01-01`, \"Before this year\" is `modified < 2026-01-01`, differing only by\noperator), so tracking by value would make removing one chip drop both."],[961,"a click **replaces all the applied filters** by the quick filter's own, and keeps the rest of the query — the text above all;"],[1047,"A click has applied this quick filter."],[1017,"A click on a quick filter **replaces** the active filters by its own, closes the popover and announces it. The list is\nsearchable and each row says how many filters it holds; hovering (or focusing) a row shows them as chips in a card under it, each as the icon the application gave the aggregation of the filter (the `icon` of the \"filters\" custom JSON, as on the filter button) and the value; an aggregation without an icon keeps its name."],[2278,"a click on the send button, or Enter pressed while it has the focus;"],[2913,"A click or a tap anywhere outside the tooltip and its host closes it too. It is what makes a tooltip usable on a touch\nscreen, where nothing hovers and no keyboard focus ever comes: give the information a button that opens it\nwith `show()` (`#tip=\"tooltip\"`, then `(click)=\"tip.isOpen() ? tip.hide() : tip.show()\"`), and the next tap\nelsewhere closes it. The listener is armed one task after the tooltip opens, so the click of that button never\ncloses what it has just opened, and a second tap on it closes the tooltip without reopening it."],[724,"A cloud needs space: words that find no room are dropped rather than shown overlapping, and the count is\nsurfaced so the omission is never silent."],[883,"A collapsible accordion of facets for a sidebar or drawer, with keyboard navigation jumping directly between facet headers."],[62,"A collapsible app navigation panel, for the shell around pages like this one."],[2967,"A collapsible app navigation panel, with an automatic mobile drawer."],[1401,"A collapsible metadata panel to place above the preview."],[1293,"A collapsible metadata panel with caller-projected rows."],[2440,"A color is never the only carrier of information (WCAG 1.4.1). Pair the bullet with a text label, or give it\nan `aria-label` when there genuinely is no label next to it. Do not put text inside a bullet either — its\nsize is fixed and content would be clipped; write the label as a sibling instead."],[2429,"A colored dot showing a status, category or priority next to a label — the dot half of Badge, without the content."],[2448,"A colored status dot, the undressed half of Badge."],[1208,"A compatibility bridge for a legacy `Text[lang]Translation` syntax that predates Angular i18n — most\napplications never author strings in this format themselves, but the server still returns some. Impure by\ndesign: it re-evaluates on every `TranslocoService.langChanges$` emission, not only on a new input value, so a\nlabel already on screen updates when the user switches language without any component code reacting to it."],[3007,"A component projected inside `sidebarHeader`/`sidebarContent`/`sidebarFooter` reads the panel's own state by\ninjecting `SIDEBAR_REF` — the same token `SidebarTriggerDirective` itself resolves through."],[2699,"A confirmation prompt, an edit form, a notice that needs an explicit dismissal — each of those is a window\nthat has to sit above the rest of the page, trap focus while it is open, and hand a result back to whoever\nopened it. `Dialog` is that window, built on the native HTML `<dialog>` element (or a `[dialog]` attribute on\nany other host), and `createCallable`/`injectCallRef` is the typed call/result API most of this page teaches."],[738,"A controlled date facet, with a live selection"],[355,"A current/new/confirm password form that signs the user back in on success, so the session is never left stale — used both as the /login?mode=changepassword route and embedded in a profile panel."],[1948,"A custom \"Promoted\" badge"],[656,"A date aggregation's buckets, plotted as a stepped line with an optional drag-to-select brush — replacing an\n\\~800-line d3 timeline with Chart.js alone, plus a category axis and a small brush plugin."],[755,"A date column aggregated with a mask (`YYYY`, `YYYY-MM`) returns items such as `{ value: \"2016\", count: 12 }`,\nwith no `display`. The mask is deduced from the values, and the label is the value itself, formatted in the\nactive language for `YYYY-MM` (`March 2024` / `mars 2024`). Picking one commits the full dates of the period,\n`gte 2016-01-01` and `lt 2017-01-01` (December rolls over to the next year), and puts the mask in the query's\n`aggregation_overrides`, keyed by **aggregation name** (`{ Modified: { mask: \"YYYY\" } }`), which tells the server\nhow the values are built. Overrides of other aggregations are kept."],[2711,"A declarative (non-callable) dialog, using every layout slot plus the three ways to open the same `<dialog>`\nreference."],[1726,"a default that is `null` (it means \"no default\")."],[1747,"A dialog announces itself, then lets `Tab` walk in: with nothing more, a keyboard user opening the account panel\nwould press `Tab` through the close button and the panel navigation before reaching the profile they came to\nedit. So when the dialog **opens** on the account panel, the focus goes straight to its first control — the photo,\nelse the password button, else the first field. It waits for the profile to load, and never takes the focus back\nfrom a user who has already moved on."],[2160,"A directive that restyles the native `<button>` element, and a pressed/unpressed pill that works standalone\nor grouped into an exclusive or multi-selection toolbar."],[2953,"A disabled `<button>` receives no pointer events in most browsers, so nothing opens the tooltip. Put the\ndirective on a wrapper element, or use `aria-disabled=\"true\"` instead of `disabled`."],[1889,"A document can match a multi-term query without containing every term — `<missing-terms>` reads\n`article.termspresence` and shows the ones absent from this specific document, each one a link that re-runs\nthe search with that term required."],[1847,"A document's place in a hierarchy, as breadcrumbs that overflow into a dropdown."],[1828,"A document's place in a hierarchy, as clickable breadcrumb segments that navigate through an aggregation — and overflow into a dropdown when the container is too narrow."],[2643,"A drag that is abandoned — dropped outside the list, Esc — puts the items back, sends the copy home, and\nemits nothing. With reduced motion requested (`prefers-reduced-motion`), the items and the copy do not animate."],[1930,"A dropdown listing the sort choices a tab or query configuration actually offers, resolved from the current result rather than passed in by hand."],[2783,"A dropdown of actions, a \"kebab\" row menu, a nested settings menu — `Menu` composes `MenuItem`s (with optional\nnested `SubMenu`s) inside `MenuContent`, wired to a trigger with `MenuTriggerDirective`. It is itself a\npopover — opening, positioning, dismissal and focus restoration all come from the same native Popover API\nPopover is built on, applied as a host directive, so there is no `<div popover>` wrapper to\nwrite yourself."],[1844,"A dropdown of the sort choices a tab or query configuration actually offers."],[2321,"A dropdown that behaves like a native `<select>` — keyboard navigable, `aria-selected`, popup positioned near\nthe field — but accepts option and trigger content of any shape. `SelectMenu` (`SelectComponent`) covers both\nsingle and multiple selection from one component."],[817,"A facet — \"Sources\", \"Authors\", \"Modified date\" — is one **aggregation** of a query's result, rendered so the\nuser can turn a bucket into a filter with a click. `<Aggregation>` picks and renders the right shape (a flat\nlist, a tree, or a date range) for a given column, and handles selecting, applying and clearing the filter for\nyou."],[751,"A facet is often rendered in a native `popover=\"auto\"` — that is what `<filter-button>`\ndoes. The custom-range dialog is modal, and `showModal()` **hides every auto popover that is not an ancestor of\nthe dialog**. Mounted in `document.body` like any callable dialog, it would close the popover that opened it\nand destroy the facet with it, dialog included."],[872,"A facet lit from its own local selection state has to reconcile after a chip is removed elsewhere on the\npage — neither the value nor the object reference survives the round-trip (the store rebuilds entries by\nspreading them), so compare on `filterKey` instead:"],[1003,"A facet with nothing to pick and nothing applied stays in the list, dimmed and inert (`hideWhenEmpty` removes it)."],[1141,"A failing endpoint never breaks the start-up, but it delays it: the condition is what spares the backends\nwithout BFF a failed request and an extra round trip on every start-up."],[91,"A favorite is a flag on a recent search, keyed by its query text: un-favoriting never deletes the search, and\ndeleting the search drops its favorite."],[910,"A fixed placement, ignoring available space"],[108,"A floating action bar that appears once the user has multi-selected documents — add to a collection, export, or attach to an AI assistant — backed by the shared SelectionStore."],[106,"A floating bar for acting on several selected documents at once."],[2843,"A footer with actions"],[1682,"A free text, edited like any other field."],[2355,"A free-text field that turns what is typed into removable tags — comma or Enter adds one, Backspace removes the last, duplicates are ignored."],[2237,"A free-text field that turns what is typed into removable tags."],[1473,"A full-page error state with an optional detail message read from the \"message\" query param, and a way back to a fresh sign-in attempt."],[1492,"A full-page error state with an optional detail message."],[1491,"A full-screen dimming overlay, shown and hidden through a service."],[1465,"A full-screen dimming overlay, shown and hidden through BackdropService — not a settable input."],[2317,"A fully custom trigger"],[298,"A functional route guard that checks authentication, loads the principal, and redirects to change-password when a credentials session's password has expired."],[2620,"A group with no measurable size (a hidden route, `display: none`) cannot turn a pointer move into a\npercentage, and the drag is simply ignored until the group has a size again. Check that the group's parent\nactually has a height — a bare `<div>` with no height collapses the whole group to zero."],[2176,"A grouped item requires an ancestor `<ToggleGroup>` (or any `ngToolbar`) — `ToolbarWidget` resolves\n`inject(Toolbar)` through the regular element-injector hierarchy, so `<Toggle value>` items must be light-DOM\ndescendants of `<ToggleGroup>`, not children of some other wrapping component."],[1018,"A handle on the top edge of the popover (and one on the bottom edge when there is room) resizes its height, with the mouse and with the arrow keys; the height is kept while the page is open, and the popover is placed again by Floating UI (flipped, shifted) each time it opens and each time the page scrolls under it."],[2668,"A hidden gesture does not exist for a screen reader or a switch user. Keep the action reachable by a visible button\n(`pointer-coarse:sr-only` once the swipe replaces it for a sighted finger), and give the row its keyboard path as before."],[1611,"A keyboard shortcut usually means three things to get right at once: comparing the right kind of key across\nkeyboard layouts, not stealing a keystroke a text field or another component needs, and keeping a help list\nthat does not drift from what is actually registered. `KeyboardShortcutsService` is one `keydown` listener, one\nregistry, and a `[keyShortcut]` directive for the common case — built to replace an older engine that could\nnot be made correct on a non-US layout."],[2536,"A keyboard-navigable ARIA grid shell for a list of rows that hold more than one focusable control — reach for it instead of List/ListItem in that case."],[2452,"A keyboard-navigable grid for rows that need more than one focusable control."],[1538,"A labeled light/dark switch for one ThemeStore scope, built on Signal Forms' checkbox contract."],[1489,"A light/dark switch for a scope."],[1563,"A light/dark switch for a scope."],[1536,"A light/dark switch for the same scope."],[2496,"A list is a single tab stop and the arrow keys do the rest, which nothing tells a keyboard user.\n`List.keyboardFocused` is true while the keyboard focus — `:focus-visible`, so not a mouse click — is inside the\nlist, which is exactly when a hint is useful. Read it through the `list` template reference."],[572,"A menu button that lets the user like or dislike the current results, or send a typed message about content, interface, language or anything else, audited for the administrators."],[2792,"A menu entry that toggles a state cannot put a control (a checkbox, a switch) **inside** a `MenuItem`: a\n`menuitem` containing an interactive control is invalid ARIA, and it would leave that control out of the\nmenu's own keyboard navigation. The ARIA APG answer is for the item itself to carry the role and the\nstate — supported through `role=\"menuitemcheckbox\"`/`\"menuitemradio\"` plus a `checked` input, which also stops\nthe menu from closing when such an item is picked, so several options can be toggled in a row."],[1488,"A menu listing every registered theme for a scope."],[1562,"A menu of registered themes, bound to a scope."],[1528,"A menu, opened from your own trigger content, listing every registered theme for a scope and switching it on click."],[2784,"A menu's items are not each individually tabbable: `Tab` leaves the whole menu in one step, and `↓`/`↑`/`Home`/\n`End` move a single \"active\" focus between items instead. This is the ARIA **menu** pattern, and\n`@angular/aria/menu` implements all of it — the roving focus, the keyboard navigation, and typeahead — so\n`Menu` only has to compose the pieces."],[829,"A missing aggregation is a misconfiguration (a typo'd `name`, an aggregation removed from the app's setup) —\nnot a state worth showing the user anything about — so it always disappears. A facet that genuinely resolves\nto zero items is a legitimate, often temporary state, so it stays by default and only disappears once you opt\nin with `hideWhenEmpty`. Two exemptions keep a facet the user can still act on regardless of that input: a\ndate facet (no \"resolved but empty\" state exists for it — see Pitfalls) and a facet currently\ncarrying an applied filter (hiding it would leave no way to clear that filter from the facet itself)."],[1808,"A mixed result — some terms corrected, others expanded — deliberately falls back to `suggestion`: it is the\nonly one of the three messages that does not assert a specific search behavior that may not actually have\nhappened for every term."],[2838,"A modal panel anchored to one edge of the viewport — the drawer pattern — built on the same native <dialog> as Dialog, with its own slide-in/out animation and scroll lock."],[2765,"A modal panel anchored to one edge of the viewport — the drawer pattern — sharing Dialog's tokens."],[2806,"A modal window with the same imperative call/result API, for content heavier than a menu."],[1370,"A native (auto) popover would close on a click into the field that owns it, and on a click on one of its own\ntabs, which takes the focus out of the field. The panel is `popover=\"manual\"` instead: it opens on the field's\nfocus, and the bar closes it on Escape, on a press outside the panel and the field, and when the\nwindow loses the focus (a press inside the iframe)."],[2965,"A native anchor styled as a navigation link, internal or external."],[2338,"A native checkbox styled as an on/off track-and-thumb toggle, with the same Signal Forms shape as Checkbox."],[2209,"A native checkbox wrapped in an accessible label, with an indeterminate visual state and Signal Forms integration."],[2239,"A native input wrapped in a styled flex container that drives its focus, disabled and read-only look purely from the input's own state, with optional icon slots and a character counter."],[2252,"A native radio input wrapped in an accessible label, grouped by a shared name and a derived selection signal rather than a container component."],[2378,"A native textarea wrapped like Input, with three height strategies and a rows-independent min/max bound for content-driven auto-sizing."],[3039,"A navigation panel that composes many of the same accessibility patterns."],[1718,"A nested property, like a leaf: `\"agent/favorites\"` is `favorites` under `agent`, at any depth."],[685,"A one-dimensional aggregation as a wrapping list of tags — the lightweight option."],[375,"A one-field form that requests a password-reset email — no router, no navigation, safe to drop into a dialog or a wizard step as-is."],[404,"A one-field reset-email request, safe to embed anywhere."],[514,"A page to manage collections, with a detail view and an apply-to-filters action."],[521,"A page to manage collections: grid or list, create, delete, a detail view, and applying one to the filters."],[461,"A page to manage the user's collections — grid or list, filter, create, delete — with a detail view of one collection (rename it, preview its documents) and an action that applies it to the filters."],[520,"A paginated list of the user's collections, with add-to-collection and delete dialogs."],[497,"A paginated list of the user's saved collections (baskets), with an add-to-collection dialog and a delete confirmation — built on the shared ListPanel primitives."],[2796,"A panel that is not a `Menu` — a listbox of search results, a custom popover — can wear the same surface through the\nclass helpers the `Menu` itself is built from: `menuPanelVariants()` (rounded, shadowed, padded panel),\n`menuItemVariants()` (a row, with hover, active and disabled states), `menuContentVariants()` and\n`menuSeparatorVariants()`. They only return class names; the behaviour — roles, keyboard, positioning — stays yours."],[2844,"A panel with no visible title"],[2568,"A pastille apposed on another element — a counter or a status icon — rather than an inline chip."],[2447,"A pastille apposed on another element — a counter or a status icon."],[1729,"A path declared in both `customData` and `privateCustomData` gives two rows, in two cards: they are two distinct\nvalues on the server."],[2184,"A people picker"],[1012,"A pill that opens the user's named sets of filters, to apply them again in one click."],[2164,"A pill-shaped pressed/unpressed button, standalone or grouped into a segmented control built on @angular/aria/toolbar."],[2826,"A popover lives in the browser's top layer, so no ancestor clips it: when its trigger scrolls out of the list or\ncontainer it sits in, the popover keeps floating over nothing. `[hideWhenTriggerHidden]=\"true\"` hides it\n(`visibility: hidden`, it stays open) while the trigger is out of sight, and shows it again when the trigger comes back."],[2911,"A press on the host (`pointerdown`, `click`) closes the tooltip, and the focus that a press gives a button does\nnot open it again: only a keyboard focus does."],[2162,"A pressed/unpressed pill, standalone or as a segmented control built on @angular/aria/toolbar."],[2156,"A pressed/unpressed pill, standalone or grouped into a segmented control."],[1728,"A private property is read, saved and deleted through `api/v2/user-profile/privateCustomData/{path}` **only** — never\nthrough the public routes, nested paths included. A public property keeps using the public ones."],[1720,"A profile with custom data would be one long form, so the form is split in **tabs**, one per block: *Information* (the\n`data` fields), *Preferences* (`customData`) and *Private* (`privateCustomData`). A tab only exists when it has rows, and a\nprofile with a single block shows no tab at all. Each tab holds a card that says who can see its values (**Public** or\n**Private**). Switching tab discards an edit in progress, and the content of a tab is rendered the first time it is\nopened."],[1699,"A property with a **default value**. An object with several keys declares one property per key."],[1697,"A property with no default."],[1260,"A proxy that authenticates in front of the backend (OIDC) answers an expired session with a cross-origin redirect to the\nidentity provider. `fetch` rejects with a `TypeError` before the client sees a response, so no event is raised and\nneither signal fires. Signing in again is then up to the proxy."],[37,"A pure Angular presentation library of tokens-only components — buttons, forms, overlays, navigation — for building Sinequa search UIs."],[2427,"A read-only inline chip for categorizing content, instead of a pastille glued to another element."],[1072,"A recovery hook (`client.config.auth.recoverFromUnauthorized`) usually performs requests of its own. If one of\nthose comes back 401, the client calls the hook again — and a hook that returns the recovery already in flight\nwaits on itself, silently. Pass `noRecovery: true` on the requests your recovery makes, and have it refuse\nre-entry while a recovery is already running."],[1187,"A request either goes through the atomic client (which handles it directly) or through `HttpClient` (which\nthese interceptors cover) — never both. Registering the client's own handling *and* these interceptors is\ntherefore correct, not a duplicate."],[2330,"A rich label that `fieldLabel` cannot express goes in a projected `.select-label` element, with\n`SelectLabelDirective` in the `imports` of the declaring component: the directive gives the element an id and the\nselect names the trigger and the list from it (the projected label wins over `fieldLabel`). Without the directive\nthe element is painted but is not part of the accessible name."],[1624,"A route held by a `RouteReuseStrategy` is not destroyed on navigation, so a `[keyShortcut]` on it stays\nregistered even though the page is no longer visible. Bind `[shortcutDisabled]` to whether the route is\ncurrently active."],[1169,"A route or component subtree with its own client, stores and services."],[2797,"A row that is the current one is tinted like a hovered item: `data-active=\"true\"` for the Menu's own roving items and for\nthe options of an `@angular/aria` listbox (which mark the current row that way), `aria-selected=\"true\"` for a listbox written\nby hand following the APG."],[2663,"A row that must not swipe"],[557,"A save that fails never looks like it succeeded: the store only changes once the server has answered, the form\nkeeps what was typed and shows the reason **in the form** — a toast would sit behind a modal dialog, which is\nin the top layer."],[1555,"A scope is just a string key you choose (`\"application\"`, `\"main\"`, the id of a panel) — `ThemeStore` keeps one\nindependent theme/dark-mode pair per scope, so nesting or coexisting themes is a matter of using different scope\nnames, not a feature you configure."],[1105,"A scope re-creates the stores and services, not the application infrastructure around them. Before adding one:"],[150,"A screen reader is told differently, so that nothing is announced twice: the row carries the delete sentence as\nits description (read when the row takes focus), and the footer hint is hidden from assistive technology since the\nlistbox already announces its own navigation. All of it is translated (`en`, `fr`, `de`)."],[2294,"A search field styled like InputGroup, meant to sit inline among other form fields rather than standing alone as a pill."],[2233,"A search field styled to blend into a form."],[2195,"A search fires once the typed query, debounced, reaches `minLength` characters. Picking a suggestion empties the field and\nre-runs the search with an empty query, so the list keeps showing everything the `loader` returns (minus the applied values):\na `loader` must accept `\"\"` as \"no filter\". While it is in flight the field's\nchevron gives way to a spinner and the rows of the previous search stay on screen — replacing them with a\n\"Searching…\" line made the list blink on every keystroke — so `searchingText` only shows when there is nothing\nto keep. Only a search that has come back (empty) may claim there is nothing, and a failed one says so in an\nalert row (`errorText`). The `loader` receives an `AbortSignal`: a newer query aborts the request of the older\none — hand it to `fetch`. The popup is a manual popover in the top layer, so a dialog's edges don't clip it."],[975,"A search rarely stays a plain text query. The user ticks \"PDF only\", expands a folder in a tree, picks \"last\nmonth\" — each facet renders one aggregation of the query's result, and clicking an item turns into a filter on\nthe next query. This section covers that whole loop: rendering a facet, applying and clearing its selection,\nand showing the user what is currently filtered."],[1915,"A search that fails still resolves to a `Result` — the request never throws — with the failure captured on\n`$error` instead. An empty `records` array is ambiguous by itself: it means \"the corpus matched nothing\" on a\nsuccessful request, and \"something went wrong\" on a failed one. Check `$error` first, always."],[896,"A searchable facet does not show its search field until asked: a magnifier button in the header, next to the chevron, opens it\nwith a short slide and puts the focus in it, and closes it again — which also clears what was typed, so no filter stays on that\nyou cannot see. `Escape` in the field does the same. The field is folded and `inert` in the meantime, out of the tab order and\nof the accessibility tree. In a popover that holds one facet (no header), the magnifier is in the bar below instead."],[2234,"A self-contained pill search field with clear and send controls."],[2275,"A self-contained search field — think an application's global search — with a leading magnifier icon and\nbuilt-in clear (×) and send controls, distinct from `SearchInput` which blends into a\nform alongside other fields."],[2265,"A self-contained, pill-shaped search field with a leading icon and built-in clear/send controls, meant to stand on its own rather than inside a form."],[2878,"A sheet still needs an accessible name with no heading in the design. `ariaLabel` provides it directly and\ntakes precedence over `labelledby` and over any projected title; `closeButton` floats a close affordance for a\nfull-bleed panel that carries no `SheetHeader` at all."],[2879,"A sheet that answers a question — pick a collection, confirm an export — opens imperatively and resolves,\nexactly like a callable dialog: `createCallable` takes any standalone component, and nothing in that path\nrequires a `<dialog>` element, so a `Sheet` works with it unchanged. Wire `end()` to `closeEnd` rather than to\nthe click that closes the panel — that is what lets the exit animation play before the component is destroyed."],[2769,"A short description on hover and keyboard focus, in the top layer, with the same selector as the @sinequa/ui one."],[2894,"A short description shown next to any element on hover and keyboard focus, placed in the top layer — the galactik replacement of the @sinequa/ui tooltip directive."],[81,"A side panel listing the user's recent searches, with a switch to show only the ones marked as favorite."],[614,"A Sinequa aggregation as a bar, pie or doughnut chart, on Chart.js — an optional peer dependency, from a separate entry point."],[11,"A Sinequa application typically layers three things: a **backend** (the search engine and its REST API), a\n**client** (`@sinequa/atomic`, which turns REST calls into typed queries and results), and a **UI layer**\n(this library) that renders that data as sign-in screens, facets, result lists and previews. Nothing here talks\nto the backend directly — every network call goes through `@sinequa/atomic`."],[1386,"A Sinequa index can store more than one rendered form of a document — its **conversions** (a PDF-like page\nimage, a Markdown extraction, a multi-format bundle). `<preview-content>` resolves which conversion is active\nand swaps its whole rendering strategy (iframe vs. Markdown) based on it — this is not a cosmetic detail, the\nmarkdown branch skips the iframe and `<preview-actions>`'s search/highlights entirely."],[2261,"A single `Radio` exposes exactly `checked = model<boolean>(...)`, the structural shape `FormCheckboxControl`\nrequires — so `[formField]` binds one radio to one boolean sub-field, but `FormCheckboxControl` doesn't give a\nwhole group mutual exclusivity by itself. For an exclusive choice backed by Signal Forms, keep the shared-signal\npattern from the minimal example (or wrap the group behind a custom `FormValueControl<string>`)."],[2311,"A single- or multiple-choice dropdown built on the accessible @angular/aria combobox/listbox primitives, with a fully custom trigger and option rendering when the default chrome doesn't fit."],[2235,"A single- or multiple-choice dropdown over a fixed, synchronous options list."],[61,"A single- or multiple-choice dropdown, the other half of most forms."],[2231,"A single-line text field with icon slots and a character counter."],[2168,"A single-selection segmented control"],[58,"A small form: an `Input` bound to a signal, and a `Button` that opens a confirmation `Dialog` before\n\"submitting\" — the same `createCallable`/`injectCallRef` pattern the Dialog page\nteaches in full."],[2415,"A small pastille apposed on another element — a numeric counter or a status icon — glued on with your own positioning."],[1144,"A source does not have to provide every part. One that only knows the application configuration — cached from\na previous visit, say — answers the others with `{ ok: false }` (or leaves them out), and they are read the\nusual way, in parallel:"],[1733,"A standard field is labelled with `userProfile.data.<key>`. A free-form property is labelled with\n`userProfile.customData.<key>` (`userProfile.privateCustomData.<key>` for a private one) when the application provides that translation in the `user-profile` scope, and with\nthe key itself otherwise — so nothing needs translating for the form to work. A leaf is named after its object:\nthe label of `workingHours` followed by `› start`."],[103,"A starred toggle button on a document, and the paginated list of everything bookmarked."],[64,"A starred toggle button on any document, and a paginated list of the user's bookmarks — reopening one re-runs the query it came from to land back on the exact record."],[2552,"A static, read-only chip for categorizing content — a document type, an applied filter shown for reference, a status label."],[2446,"A static, read-only chip for categorizing content."],[191,"A suggestion or a saved search too long for its row is cut with an ellipsis, and a tooltip shows the whole text (only when it is cut)."],[1500,"A tab bar generated from the Angular Router's own child-route configuration, with automatic overflow into a dropdown and optional per-tab result counts."],[1490,"A tab bar generated straight from the router's child-route configuration."],[1510,"A tab shows no badge at all (not a `0` badge) unless its `queryName` matches the current result's query name;\nit is disabled only once the matched count is exactly `0` — in the visible bar and in the overflow menu alike."],[2366,"A tag is trimmed. An empty one is ignored, and so is a duplicate **whatever its case** — the first spelling stays."],[2561,"A tag the user can take away carries a `tag-remove` after its label: a real `<button>` (Tab to reach it, Enter or Space\nto activate it) named after the tag, with an `removed` event."],[2912,"A tap does not open it: a browser follows a tap with the pretend mouse events of a mouse (a `mouseenter` among them), and the\ntooltip ignores the one that comes after a touch `pointerdown`. A mouse, and a pen, which does hover, open it as usual."],[2898,"A template as the content"],[1706,"A text input."],[1554,"A theme is a named set of CSS custom properties — one value per color role (`primary`, `background`,\n`destructive`, …), in a light and a dark variant. `ThemeStore` holds every registered theme and, for each\n**scope** you define, which one is currently active and in which mode."],[2966,"A thin styling layer over @angular/aria/tabs."],[3019,"A thin Tailwind styling layer over Angular's official @angular/aria/tabs primitives — roles, focus and keyboard navigation come entirely from Angular."],[648,"A time series with a drag-to-select range brush, on Chart.js — no d3, no date adapter, gap-filled buckets."],[629,"A time series with a drag-to-select range brush, on the same ChartCanvas foundation."],[696,"A time series with a drag-to-select range brush."],[1082,"A toast here is a `notify.error(…)` call from `@sinequa/atomic`, which only dispatches a `notification`\n`CustomEvent` on `window`. Nothing in `@sinequa/atomic-angular` or `@sinequa/galactik` listens to that event: your\napplication must provide a toaster (a bridge from the event to your toast component). Without one, no toast is\never visible."],[609,"A toast here is a `notify.error(…)` call, which only dispatches a `notification` `CustomEvent` on `window`:\nnothing in the library renders it, your application must provide a toaster listening to that event."],[926,"A toolbar listing the facets a user can filter on — one popover button per aggregation, with overflow handled by a \"More\" button."],[2957,"A tooltip opens on the focus of its host. A label inside a list row or a card is not focusable — the row is — so\nthe keyboard never reaches the tooltip, and a sighted keyboard user would never read the cut part. Do not move the\ntooltip to the focusable row either: its `aria-describedby` would make a screen reader read the label twice. Lift\nthe cut while the row has the focus instead, for instance `in-focus-visible:line-clamp-none` (and\n`in-focus-visible:whitespace-normal` on a one-line `truncate`). The full text is always in the DOM: a screen\nreader reads it whole whether or not it is cut on screen."],[3003,"A trailing `Badge` is pinned to the end of an item and dropped automatically once the\nsidebar is icon-only — there is no room next to a bare icon for a pill."],[2917,"A truncated label (`truncate`, `line-clamp-2`) hides part of its text, and a tooltip is the natural way to give it back —\nbut a tooltip on a label that fits only repeats it. `TruncatedDirective` (`[truncated]`) measures the element and\nexposes `isTruncated()` through `exportAs=\"truncated\"`: bind its negation to `tooltipDisabled`."],[674,"A two-dimensional distribution — documents by source **and** by format, say — needs more than a list: a\nheatmap shows both axes at once, with colour standing in for count. `<Heatmap>` renders it as a CSS grid,\nwhich is what lets every cell and every axis label be a real, clickable, keyboard-reachable `<button>`."],[692,"A two-dimensional distribution as a CSS grid — no dependency, accessible, clickable axis labels."],[630,"A two-dimensional distribution on canvas, for matrices too large for the DOM."],[2450,"A user or entity, as a picture or initials, with an automatic fallback."],[1977,"A user-managed set of documents — listed, opened, uploaded into, shared and previewed — as Angular components, with a custom-element build for pages that are not Angular."],[931,"A vertical bar, for a sidebar layout"],[351,"A view being torn down as the router leaves the page, a save already in flight, a telemetry event — all of\nthem can reach the server moments later, on a cookie that has just been deleted, and answer 401. Nothing\nrecovers from those: `@sinequa/atomic` (2.3.2+) closes the recovery from a deliberate `logout()` until the\nnext successful authentication, and `signIn()` refuses to redirect away from an authentication screen. Without\neither, the audit event's 401 re-probed the session, found it gone, and replaced the \"signed out\" confirmation\nwith `/login?returnUrl=/logout` — signing back in then returned the user to the logout page."],[2522,"A WAI-ARIA feed of articles for a list of cards that grows as the user scrolls — reach for it instead of RowGrid when the list is not a table."],[2453,"A WAI-ARIA feed of articles, for a list of cards that grows as the user scrolls."],[2037,"A workspace has no \"favorites\" notion yet, so there is no such category. `predicate` is where one would plug in."],[997,"Above 6 overflow filters, `<More>` itself grows a facet-name search box, independently of which container it\nrenders inside — a popover with many facets is otherwise as hard to scan as a sidebar with many facets."],[257,"Access and people"],[1303,"Accessibility"],[2341,"Accessible name without a label"],[1809,"Action"],[1326,"Add a button that never goes into the menu"],[1325,"Add actions that may overflow"],[1355,"Add an app-specific action"],[1136,"Add it only when the application is actually served behind such an endpoint. Against a Sinequa server reached\ndirectly, it brings nothing and costs a round trip on every start-up: the request answers `404`, a warning is\nlogged, and only then do the parallel reads start. Those parallel reads are the default — they need no\nprovider."],[2733,"Add the equivalent for the manual backdrop `<div>` too, if you stack `[dialog]` attribute hosts."],[495,"Add the selected documents to a collection."],[1725,"adding or removing a key of an object;"],[1190,"Adds Sinequa's audit metadata to a request body, for any request whose URL contains `api/v1` and whose body is\nJSON-serializable (skipped for `HttpParams` bodies). The `@sinequa/atomic` API functions already add this to\ntheir own requests; this covers the ones built directly on `HttpClient`."],[1188,"Adds the current interface language to the request body as `ui-language`, read fresh from `TranslocoService`\non **every** request rather than captured once — the language changes while the application runs (the user\nmenus and the user-profile form call `setActiveLang`), and a request must carry the one in force when it is\nsent. `FormData` bodies get the field appended directly; a plain object body is cloned with the field added.\n`GET`/`HEAD` requests pass through untouched — they carry no body with the `fetch` backend."],[1071,"Adopt `injectAtomicClient()` everywhere once a client is provided; do not mix free functions and a provided\nclient in the same application."],[2645,"Adopt the new order at once and put the previous one back if the request fails: the list shown follows the list\nyou gave, so a drop keeps its result on screen while the request is in flight."],[3,"Agent skills are packaged instructions that an AI coding agent loads on demand. Two skills ship with this\nrepository and target **consumers** of the libraries, not contributors: they teach the agent the public API,\nconventions and pitfalls of `@sinequa/atomic-angular` and `@sinequa/galactik`."],[803,"Aggregation"],[613,"Aggregation Chart"],[729,"Aggregation date"],[631,"Aggregation Heatmap"],[856,"Aggregation icon instead of its name"],[647,"Aggregation Timeline"],[693,"Aggregation values as a wrapping list of tags, sized by count."],[713,"Aggregation values packed into a compact spiral layout — large words centered, smaller ones tucked into the gaps, some rotated."],[699,"Aggregation values rendered as a wrapping list of tags sized by count — the lightweight default, with no layout algorithm and no canvas."],[1,"AI agent skills"],[541,"Alerts"],[1984,"All of them read the same `WorkspacesStore`, so a change made in one — a role changed from \"Manage access\", a\nstatus patched by the upload flow — shows in the others without anything being pushed."],[627,"Almost always a container with no resolved height — Chart.js sizes the canvas from its parent's box. Give the\nhost (or its wrapper) an explicit height, as the examples on this page do with `class=\"h-64\"`."],[922,"Also a regression to report, not expected — the component closes its own popover on `focusout` once focus\ngenuinely leaves the button and its panel (checked via `contains()` on the `relatedTarget`). A `null`\n`relatedTarget` — focus leaving the document entirely (alt-tab, browser chrome) — is the one case where it is\ndeliberately left open, so it survives a window switch."],[611,"Also deliberate — `api/v2/user-profile` requests are excluded so the caller (typically a form) can show the\nerror inline instead of as a transient toast."],[826,"Always hidden, unconditionally"],[2950,"Always in the top layer, above dialogs"],[818,"An **aggregation** is a bucketed count over one column of the result set — how many documents have each\nvalue of `docformat`, how many fall in each date range of `modified`. The server computes it alongside the\nresult records; `<Aggregation>` never computes it itself, only renders and lets the user filter on it."],[1880,"An `iconPath` renders an `<img>`; otherwise `iconClass` is applied to an `<i>` element."],[3011,"An `InjectionToken<SidebarRef>` a `<Sidebar>` provides for anything projected into it, exposing `collapsed`,\n`isMobile`, `expanded` (all `Signal<boolean>`) and `toggle()`/`open()`/`close()` — the last three branch on\n`isMobile()` automatically (desktop collapse vs. the mobile drawer)."],[2771,"An accessible dropdown or contextual menu built on @angular/aria — roving focus, typeahead, unlimited nested submenus, and checkable items with no interactive control inside a menuitem."],[2766,"An accessible dropdown/contextual menu with nested submenus and checkable items."],[2892,"An accessible dropdown/contextual menu, itself built as a popover."],[2469,"An accessible list of selectable rows built on @angular/aria/listbox, with composable slots for content lists, action menus and navigation lists."],[2451,"An accessible list of selectable rows, built on @angular/aria/listbox."],[2413,"An adjacent role/category label to pair with an avatar in a member row."],[937,"An aggregation becomes a filter button only if the app's `filters` customization JSON lists it — an entry\nmatched against the aggregation by `name` when it has one, by `column` otherwise — and the admin has not marked it\n`hidden`. The bar excludes only entries whose `position` is `\"left\"`: an entry with no `position`, or with `\"both\"`,\nshows in the bar (`<aside-filters>` is the one that takes `\"left\"` and `\"both\"`, and ignores an entry with no\n`position`). Resolving that list is `AggregationsService.getAuthorizedFilters` — the bar and `<more-button>` call\nthrough it; `<aside-filters>` applies the same `hidden` rule on its own list."],[552,"An alert is a saved query the server re-runs on a schedule — a frequency, the weekdays it repeats on, a time of\nday. `<Alerts>` lists them (name and schedule on each row), switches them on or off, reorders and deletes them;\n`AlertForm` opens the dialog that creates or edits one, and `<alert-form>` is the same form without the dialog, for\nany other container."],[53,"An Angular 22 workspace with Tailwind CSS v4 already set up. `@sinequa/galactik` declares three peer\ndependencies — install them alongside it:"],[1219,"An Angular route resolver that supplies the application's default query name to a route with no explicit one."],[2987,"An app navigation panel — collapsible to an icon rail on desktop, a native-dialog drawer below the mobile breakpoint — with no rail and no nested submenus."],[1573,"An application customizes its behavior mostly through the `general` object of its JSON configuration (a\ntop-level `general` key, or a `general` customJSON side-file) — read once through `AppStore.general()`. This\npage is the one place that lists every key of `general.features`/`general.feedback` **and says which ones a\nconsumer actually checks**, since a name in the type is not a promise that anything reads it."],[2944,"An arrow by default (`[tooltipArrow]=\"false\"` removes it)"],[1848,"An article field as a row of tags, and the icon identifying which source or collection it came from."],[1149,"An audit event fired in the moments after a logout can land on the deleted session cookie, answer 401, and\nre-trigger `signIn()` — signing the user back in to a login form they deliberately left. `bootstrapApp` refuses\nrecovery for `api/v1/audit.notify` specifically, and for any request while a sign-in is already in flight (a\nrecovery that waited on its own in-flight sign-in would never settle). Both guards are already built in; if you\nsee this with a different endpoint, mark that request `noRecovery: true` rather than trying to special-case it\nhere."],[135,"An automatically populated, paginated list of the user's past searches — the same shape as saved searches, with nothing to save explicitly."],[2178,"An editable combobox for debounced backend search with multi-selection — labels, filter facets, people pickers — where picked values render as removable chips inside the field."],[2820,"An element with a `popover` attribute renders in the browser's **top layer** — above everything else, no\n`z-index` required — and is shown/hidden by the browser itself: native focus handling, `Escape`-to-close and\nclick-outside dismissal all come from the platform. `PopoverDirective` adds what the platform does not:\ncomputed placement relative to a trigger, collision-aware repositioning, and a couple of small ergonomics the\nraw attribute leaves to you."],[486,"An empty name is reported only once **Create** is pressed, not when the field loses the focus (leaving it for\n**Cancel** is not an error). A name that is already taken is reported as it is typed, whatever its case."],[192,"An empty search is refused, with a notification, when the query does not allow it."],[1693,"An entry is one of two shapes, and the two can be mixed in the same list:"],[887,"An explicit, developer-chosen facet list"],[599,"An HttpInterceptorFn that turns a failed HttpClient request into a toast for the status codes worth telling the user about, without wrapping HttpClient itself."],[845,"An inline object literal on `[aggregation]` — `[aggregation]=\"{ ...agg, display: label }\"` — is a **new\nreference on every change-detection pass**, and any reference change reseeds the whole instance (discarding\nload-more pages and open tree nodes). It also fails to compile: the raw `Aggregation` type from\n`@sinequa/atomic` has no `display` field, so the literal trips the excess-property check."],[2222,"An on/off toggle with the same Signal Forms shape as Checkbox."],[2230,"An on/off track-and-thumb toggle."],[2763,"An overlay is anything that renders above the rest of the page and captures focus or dismissal on its own\nterms: a modal dialog, an edge-anchored sheet, a dropdown menu, a floating popover. `@sinequa/galactik`'s\noverlays share the same scrim tokens (`--scrim-base`, `--blur-xs`) and, wherever the platform allows it, the\nnative top layer — so none of them need an application-level `z-index` to stack correctly above ordinary\ncontent."],[2289,"Angular hoists a `slot=\"trailing\"` marker onto a block only when that block has a single root node. Putting the\nmarker on an element that is itself inside an `@if`/`@for`, or beside a `@let`, breaks the hoist (the compiler\nreports `NG8011`) and the content lands in the default slot instead. Put the marker on an `<ng-container>`\nwrapping the whole block:"],[2322,"Angular Signal Forms recognizes a component as a form control when it exposes a `value` model matching the\n`FormValueControl<TValue>` contract. `SelectMenu` implements it through its own `value` model, so `[formField]`\nworks exactly like it would on a native input — no adapter needed."],[811,"Announce a state the row only shows visually"],[3040,"Another @angular/aria-backed composite widget, for selecting rows instead of switching panels."],[2520,"Another @angular/aria-backed composite widget, for switching between panels instead of selecting rows."],[2467,"Another component driven entirely by keyboard interaction, this one via @angular/aria."],[2476,"Another icon, another key"],[2624,"Another panel-composition component, collapsible rather than resizable."],[1893,"Another per-document component — where it sits in a collection hierarchy."],[1881,"Another small, configuration-driven display component."],[1956,"Another small, configuration-driven display component."],[2571,"Answer one question as a signal — is the viewport narrower than the md breakpoint? — for structural choices CSS cannot express."],[1418,"any other `<tr>`"],[1113,"Anything calling a **free function** (`fetchQuery()`, `login()`, `globalConfig.…`) runs on the default client,\nwhatever subtree it sits in — inside a scope, that means querying the *first* backend, silently, since the\nrequest still succeeds. Audit your own components for those calls; the library's own code never makes them."],[2579,"Anything that is purely a matter of layout belongs in a Tailwind `md:` variant instead: the CSS costs nothing\nat runtime, needs no injection, and cannot fall out of sync with the service."],[182,"API"],[1015,"API"],[1304,"API"],[2949,"Appended to the closest `<dialog>` or `body`"],[849,"Applied filters"],[466,"Apply a collection from your own component"],[465,"Apply a collection yourself"],[1518,"Apply a scope's active theme to one element and everything under it, as CSS custom properties — nestable, so a page can mix several themes."],[1561,"Apply a scope's theme to one element (and everything under it), nestable."],[1487,"Apply a scope's theme to one element and everything under it — nestable."],[473,"Applying a collection means opening `/search?b=<name>`: the search 