e` and the URL. Set\nany of `query`, `aggregation` or `selection` to switch the whole instance to **controlled mode**: it then\nreads only from those inputs, holds its own state, and never touches the shared stores, the URL or\n`sessionStorage` — changes surface exclusively through `(selectionChange)`/`(filtersChange)`. This is what lets\nseveral independent facet instances coexist on one page, each over its own query."],[2424,"By default `Badge` carries no ARIA role at all. Plain text content (a digit) is still read because it is real\ntext, but an `icon` badge's SVG typically carries `aria-hidden=\"true\"` of its own — which makes the whole\nbadge invisible to assistive technology unless you opt in. Set `aria-label`: the host then gets `role=\"img\"`\nand the given name, so the icon and its chrome are announced as one meaningful unit."],[2825,"By default `flip()`/`shift()` reposition the popover if the viewport runs out of room. `[lockPosition]=\"true\"`\ndisables both, forcing it to stay at the exact configured `placement` — useful when a consuming component\nalready accounts for available space itself and a repositioning popover would fight that logic."],[281,"By default a person picked in the search joins the readers. `roleSelector` puts the Owner / Reader selector in the\nsearch box, as the workspaces' share dialog does: whoever is picked gets the role chosen there."],[584,"By default the button carries a close cross: it is a suggestion the user can dismiss, and `onClose` tells you to\nhide it. When the button belongs to the page, remove the cross with `[dismissible]=\"false\"`, and use `size=\"sm\"`\nto match compact neighbours."],[893,"By default this renders every `\"left\"`/`\"both\"` aggregation from the app's JSON configuration (excluding\nadmin-`hidden` ones), each collapsed, one open at a time (`exclusive`, the native `<details name>` behaviour)."],[2485,"By default, `selectionMode=\"follow\"` means moving keyboard focus (arrow keys) immediately changes the\nselection — the listbox default. Set `selectionMode=\"explicit\"` (paired with `multi`, typically) whenever a\nrow also carries its own interactive affordance like `ListItemAction`, since \"select on focus\" would otherwise\nfight with reaching that action."],[645,"By design — canvas rendering is opaque to assistive technology and to text selection, and no plugin restores\neither. If accessibility matters more than raw cell count, use `<Heatmap>` instead; if the\nmatrix is genuinely too large for a DOM grid, this trade-off is the one to accept."],[1278,"By design — it returns `undefined` on every error path rather than rethrowing, logging the error instead (plus\na toast on `401`). If the caller needs to distinguish failure from a legitimately empty result, call the\nunderlying `fetch`/API function directly and handle the rejection yourself instead of wrapping it in\n`withFetch`."],[1625,"By design — the registry is one stack per combination, last registration wins, and a duplicate logs a warning\nin development mode. If both are meant to be reachable, use different combinations; if one is meant to\ntemporarily override the other (a panel opening over a page), this is the intended behavior — the covered one\ncomes back once the covering one unregisters."],[967,"By design while no filter is applied: a quick filter with no filter would apply nothing. The count it checks is that of the\nvalues of the query's filters (`QueryParamsStore.filters()`), a group being counted through the filters it holds."],[2954,"By design: the first `Escape` dismisses the tooltip and is `preventDefault`-ed, so the native `cancel` of the\n`<dialog>` does not fire; a second `Escape` closes the dialog. Set `[hideOnEscape]=\"false\"` to opt out."],[901,"By design. The `<summary>` row has `tabindex=\"-1\"`, so it never takes the keyboard focus, and facet headers\nare not wired into a grid: the arrow keys belong to the facet's own content (a listbox, a tree, a radio\ngroup). Reach the chevron with `Tab` and collapse the facet with it — a facet that is\nnot `collapsible` has no chevron because there is nothing to toggle."],[773,"calendar surface and text"],[169,"Calling `SavedSearch` directly — rather than through the popover — is useful from a custom \"save\" action that\nis not a starred toggle."],[2710,"Calling a callable more than once mounts independent, concurrently open instances rather than replacing the\nprevious one — `DialogService.call()` stacks by design, which is what lets `injectCallRef().index()` and\n`.stackSize()` drive position-aware UI in a stacked notification (see Recipes)."],[2713,"Calling a callable several times in a row mounts independent, concurrently open instances rather than\nreplacing the previous one. `injectCallRef()` exposes `index()`/`stackSize()` for position-aware UI, and\n`ended()` for driving an exit-animation state while teardown is pending. `call(props, options)` also accepts\nan explicit `injector` — useful when `provideCallable()` was not registered, or from a lazily-loaded\nsubtree — an `unmountDelay` that leaves time for a CSS exit transition before the component is destroyed, and a\n`container` that changes where the dialog is mounted (next recipe)."],[2880,"Cancelling resolves with `undefined`, since `picked` was never set — the promise always settles, whichever way\nthe panel closed, `Escape` and a scrim click included. Reach for this only when the panel's *purpose* is to\nproduce an answer for its caller; a panel driven by state that lives elsewhere (a preview bound to the current\nselection) has no result to await, and a declarative `<Sheet>` fits better there."],[1614,"Capture phase, deliberately: several components in this library stop propagation on `keydown` of their own\n(`ngCombobox` on Enter and the arrows, a galactik `ListItem` on Delete, dialogs on Escape) — a bubble-phase\nlistener would be at their mercy. The service only ever consumes an event once a registration actually\nmatches, so it does not steal a key a component below it wants."],[402,"Carries the session on the Angular HttpClient channel, which the atomic client never sees."],[380,"Carrying the username from a previous wizard step"],[823,"Case"],[1275,"Catches the callback's rejection and logs it; on a `401` it also shows a warning toast and, if an `injector`\nwas passed, re-triggers the sign-in flow. Returns `undefined` on any error rather than rethrowing — check for\n`undefined` at the call site instead of wrapping the call in `try`/`catch`."],[354,"Change Password"],[2020,"Change the look of the search box and the button"],[1577,"Changes apply to the current session only — nothing is persisted back to the backend configuration — which is\nwhat makes the tool suitable for testing a behavior without touching the deployment."],[682,"Check `encoding` against how the aggregation was actually configured on the server first — a `\"separator\"`\naggregation parsed with `{ kind: \"cross\" }` produces no valid cells, and `<Heatmap>` has no way to detect the\nmismatch on its own. A faint, uniform grey grid with no data-colored cells is the same symptom as a missing\naggregation: nothing parsed."],[1580,"Check it against the tables above first: `editablepartition`, `advancedSearch` and `expandPreview` are\nall editable here because they exist in the `CFeatures` type, but no consumer in this\nlibrary reads them — toggling them only changes the stored configuration value, with no observable effect.\nThis was confirmed by searching the library's sources for a reader of each key, not assumed from the name."],[1236,"Check its `path` was actually registered on `ROUTE_COMPONENTS` — `ApplicationService.createRoutes()` falls back\nsilently to the layout component (`isRoot: true`) for any tab whose path has no matching entry, which reads as\nthe wrong content rather than an error."],[458,"Check that navigation actually attached a `returnUrl` — `signInAgain()` always sets one, so this usually means\na custom router configuration stripped or overrode the query params on the way to `/login`."],[644,"Check that nothing overrode `options.events` on a custom configuration passed further down the chain — the\nsame event-list requirement `<AggregationTimeline>`'s brush has does not apply\nhere (the axis-click plugin uses a different hookup), but a heavily customized chart configuration can still\ninterfere with hit testing. Confirm first with the defaults, then reintroduce customization incrementally."],[2984,"Check that something is actually setting `aria-current=\"page\"` — `Link` never sets it itself. The supported\npath is `routerLinkActive` + `[ariaCurrentWhenActive]=\"'page'\"`; setting it by hand elsewhere risks fighting\nthe router for ownership of the same attribute."],[944,"Check the `filters` customization JSON first: the aggregation must be listed there (matched by `name`, else by\n`column`) — it is a whitelist. Then check its `position`: the bar excludes only `\"left\"`, so an entry with no\n`position` or with `\"both\"` shows in the bar, while a `\"left\"` facet lives in the drawer, never the bar. The admin\n`hidden` rule is applied on top of that. These checks happen in `AggregationsService.getAuthorizedFilters`, shared\nwith `<more-button>` — if the facet is missing from the bar, the \"More\" menu and `<aside-filters>`, the\nconfiguration is the first thing to check, not the component."],[921,"Check the aggregation actually has items — `disabled` follows `!agg?.items?.length`, **unless** the column is\na date column, which is never disabled even with zero buckets (a date's custom range stays usable regardless,\nthe same exemption `<aggregation-date>` itself has — see\nits pitfall)."],[899,"Check the input is bound with brackets (`[collapsible]=\"false\"`), not passed as a bare attribute\n(`collapsible`) — a bare attribute is always truthy. The same applies to `collapsed`, `exclusive` and\n`hideWhenEmpty`, all `booleanAttribute`-transformed inputs."],[1215,"Check t