gap` between siblings. There is no built-in \"no filters applied\" placeholder;\nrender your own conditionally on the chip count if you need one."],[1087,"Deliberate: only `400`, `403`, `500` and `503` are worth interrupting the user. Handle the rejected promise in the\ncalling code (a \"not found\" state, a retry) for any other failure."],[568,"Deliberate: the deletion is sent when the \"Undo\" notice goes away, not when the cross is clicked, nor when the row is\ndragged to the left on a touch screen (where the cross is out of sight, still there for a screen reader). Closing the\npopover that hosts the list sends it at once, so nothing is lost; only a closed tab or a crash in those six\nseconds keeps the alert."],[567,"Deliberate. A disabled `submit` never fires `submit()`, which is what marks every field touched and reveals\nvalidation messages — and the weekday `<fieldset>` has no other way to become touched, since its checkboxes\ncannot blur the group. Leaving Confirm enabled is what lets a user discover which field is missing. (It is\ndisabled while a save is in progress, through `form.saving()`.)"],[2653,"Deliberate. The shortcut only works while the item itself has the focus: Alt + arrows inside an input or a button\nof the item are theirs."],[1515,"Depends on the app-wide `general.features.persistFiltersAcrossTabs` flag. When it is off (the default), tab\nnavigation replaces the query params from scratch — filters, sort, selected id and page are explicitly cleared.\nTurn the flag on to merge instead, keeping those params across a tab change."],[1495,"Deprecated — three waving dots shown while the application initialized at a dedicated /loading route. Authentication now happens at bootstrap instead."],[198,"Description"],[241,"Description"],[1025,"Description"],[1044,"Description"],[2686,"Dialog"],[1797,"Did You Mean"],[1820,"Did you mean: **Catalon**?"],[739,"Disable the custom range entirely"],[788,"disabled days"],[2442,"Display"],[214,"Distance in pixels 