ch `<radio>` owns an independent `checked` model — grouping relies on two things working together: the\nnative `name` attribute (native focus/keyboard roving, and the browser visually unchecking siblings), and\nderiving every radio's `[checked]` from one shared signal so the app's own state stays authoritative. As long\nas `[checked]` is a derived expression (`selected() === 'x'`) rather than an independent local boolean per\nradio, a sibling recomputes to `false` automatically when another one is picked — the native `(change)` only\nfires on the newly-selected radio, never on the one that gets unchecked, and this is what makes that safe."],[2507,"each action still draws its own hint line on keyboard focus, so a focused row would advertise a key that does\nnothing."],[2531,"Each article carries `aria-posinset` and `aria-setsize` (`ariaRowCount` when the source reports a total, else\nthe rendered length), and the feed carries `aria-busy` while `busy` is set."],[939,"Each button opens its aggregation in a popover — see Filter button. Once more filters\nare authorized than `filtersCount` allows, the remaining ones move into the \"More\" button rather than\noverflowing the toolbar."],[348,"Each calls `signIn()` and replays the original request at most once — an `AUTH_RETRIED` context guard\nprevents an infinite loop on the interceptor side. Some requests never trigger a recovery at all: audit\nevents (fire-and-forget telemetry), the sign-in's own probes (their 401 is the answer being asked for), and\nanything trailing behind a deliberate `logout()` (see below). `signIn()` also never redirects when the user\nis already on an authentication screen — they are already where they belong."],[125,"each collection has one button — `+` adds the selected documents, `✓` means they are all there (clicking it\nremoves them); a collection that holds only part of them keeps the `+` and says so under its name;"],[895,"Each facet is a native `<details>`/`<summary>`. The `<summary>` row is **not** a keyboard stop (`tabindex=\"-1\"`):\n`Tab` goes straight to the chevron button that collapses the facet, then on to the facet's content. The chevron button is\nthe keyboard way to collapse a facet, and it exposes `aria-expanded`; clicking the row with a pointer still toggles it."],[1110,"Each panel then runs its own search, with its own stores, against its own backend. Two instances of the\n*same* component cannot be configured differently, though — Angular resolves `providers` per component\n**type**, before any `input()` exists. Write one thin wrapper per backend, each with its own literal\nconfiguration, both delegating to a shared presentational component."],[1890,"Each rendered term's query params force that term into the search (rather than replacing it), so clicking one\nbroadens the current query instead of starting a new one."],[842,"Each row (the list's `option`, the tree's `treeitem`) is named by an `aria-label` the component sets, and an\n`aria-label` replaces the row's content in its accessible name — `sr-only` included. Use `itemDescription`\ninstead (see Recipes): it goes through `aria-describedby`, which the `aria-label` does not override."],[833,"Each row carries an `aria-label` (its name), which replaces whatever the row renders in the accessible name — so a\n\"not applied yet\" mark drawn inside an `aggregationItem` template, even as `sr-only` text, is never read. Give\n`itemDescription` a callback instead: a non-empty string is exposed through `aria-describedby` on the row and\nannounced after its name."],[168,"Each row shows a badge with the number of applied filters and a relative date (\"2 days ago\"), both derived\nfrom parsing the stored URL — nothing extra to compute on the caller's side."],[1716,"Edit and delete each leaf. It is written at its path, the other leaves untouched."],[1719,"Edit and delete it, like a leaf."],[1707,"Edit and delete it. The value is saved as typed."],[1713,"Edit it as JSON — its items can be values, objects or arrays, mixed — or delete it. The text is validated before the save is offered; the whole array is written in one request."],[547,"Editing an existing alert"],[528,"Editing both label fields for one document"],[1724,"editing the items of an array one by one (an array is edited as JSON, as a whole);"],[1939,"Either way, a choice whose `orderByClause` includes `globalrelevance` is filtered out when the result has no\nrelevance score (`!result().hasRelevance`) — a relevance sort makes no sense without one."],[424,"Embedded in a dialog or a wizard step"],[359,"Embedded in a panel"],[2808,"Enhance the native HTML Popover API with Floating UI positioning — the bare primitive Menu and every other floating panel in this library are built from."],[2279,"Enter pressed in the field (plain bar only). It is not emitted while an IME composition is running\n(that Enter validates a candidate) nor while the bar is disabled, and it is emitted for an empty\nfield too: whether an empty query means anything is up to the host. The keydown is not stopped, so a\n`(keydown.enter)` on the host still hears it."],[186,"Enter, a clicked suggestion or the send button validates the search: the component emits `searched` and navigates\nto `searchPath` (`/search` by default) with `q` (the text) and `f` (the filters) as query parameters."],[1694,"Entry"],[1472,"Error"],[988,"Escalate to a modal past a threshold"],[1362,"Escape or on a press anywhere else (a click inside the document's iframe included). Emptying the field\nlifts the search."],[2517,"Even a single-selection `List` compares `value` against a `V[]` selection model — there is no scalar shortcut.\nEvery `ListItem` needs its own `value`, since it is the row's identity in that array."],[1974,"Event names with a colon cannot be bound as `(lexiq-workspaces:workspace-created)`. Add the listener with\n`addEventListener` on the element."],[1360,"Every action here reads `previewData` and calls straight into the injected `PreviewService` — nothing about\nzoom or highlights needs wiring beyond passing the loaded data in. `<preview-content>` already does this for\nyou; use `<preview-actions>` directly only when building a preview surface of your own."],[750,"Every call mounts a fresh dialog instance and tears it down on close, so no selection survives from the last\ntime it was used. The call resolves with the picked range, or `undefined` when the dialog is dismissed (cancel,\nEscape, backdrop) — the facet then leaves its model untouched."],[1730,"Every card says who can see its values — **Public** or **Private**, with an icon and a text (and a tooltip), so the\ninformation is not carried by the icon or a colour alone."],[2096,"Every change — a role, a removal, people added — is saved at once, with the arrays the workspace holds *now*. The list\nreads the store, so it shows what the server answered, and follows a change made elsewhere. Names arrive after the\nfirst paint (the directory is asked for them), so a row can read as a raw id for a moment."],[127,"every change is saved at once. After an addition the header confirms it, the panel closes about a second\nlater, the selection is emptied (`cleared` fires) and then `addedToCollection` fires with the collection's\nname — the place to leave a \"selection mode\"."],[624,"Every chart in this entry point renders through the same `<ChartCanvas>`, which enforces four rules no caller\nhas to think about: create the Chart.js instance only after the first render (a canvas created earlier\nmeasures as 0×0); always destroy it on teardown; rebuild when the chart `type` changes (Chart.js cannot swap\ncontrollers on a live instance); and rebuild when the color theme flips (`Chart.defaults` is read once, at\nconstruction)."],[768,"Every color of the calendar is a `--vc-*` custom property set on the `date-range-calendar` element. Override\nthe ones to change **after** the `@import`, with the same selector, or scoped to one facet with a class on\n`<aggregation-date>` since the calendar is mounted inside it (`.my-facet date-range-calendar { … }`). Pointing them at galactik tokens keeps the light/dark switch for free; a raw color applies to both themes.\nThe variables are those of vanilla-calendar-pro, which remains the reference for\nwhat each one paints."],[92,"Every colour of the panel is a CSS variable with a semantic-token fallback. By default it is a plain card on the\npage's layer colour; a host retints it — to sit beside a dark sidebar, say — by setting the variables on it or on an\nancestor: `--history-panel-bg`, `-fg`, `-muted` (header and day labels), `-icon`, `-hover`, `-active` (a row), `-group`,\n`-toggle-active`, `-toggle-hover` (the All / Favorites switch), `-fav`, `-fav-hover-bg`, `-del-hover-bg`, `-del-hover-fg`,\nplus `--history-panel-width` (15.625rem) and `--history-panel-gap` (the margin on its start side while open, 0 by default)."],[690,"Every component here follows the same contract as `<Aggregation>` in controlled\nmode: it takes an `aggregation` (or `aggregations`) input, never reads or writes `QueryParamsStore` /\n`AggregationsStore`, and reports interactions through outputs. A chart is therefore interchangeable with a\nlist facet — feed it from `AggregationsStore`, from `QueryService.search()` or from `fetchQuery()`, whichever\nsuits, and wire its output back into a filter the same way."],[55,"Every component reads its colors, spacing and radii exclusively from CSS custom properties —\n`--bg-primary-base`, `--font-primary-muted`, `--radius-2xl` — never a raw Tailwind color or a shadcn utility\nclass. `@sinequa/galactik` ships **no CSS of its own**: an application declares these tokens itself, once."],[2226,"Every control in this section wraps a real native element (`<input>`, `<textarea>`, or the accessible\n`@angular/aria` combobox/listbox primitives for `Select`) and drives its visual state from CSS reading that\nnative element — never from a JavaScript class toggle. Most also implement one of Angular Signal Forms'\ncontrol contracts (`FormValueControl` or `FormCheckboxControl`), so `[formField]` works alongside plain\ntwo-way binding."],[1919,"Every facet, filter chip, sort choice and pager then works by changing the URL, and this one subscription is the\nsingle place a search starts. Without it, applying a filter updates the badges and the URL but the results stay\nas they were."],[57,"Every galactik component now renders with the correct look — there is nothing to configure per component.\nA dark variant is optional: the demo app keeps its dark-mode token overrides in a second file\n(`galactik-tokens-dark.css`), scoped under a `.dark` class, imported after the light one."],[587,"Every key of `general.feedback` is off, so `showButton` is false and the component renders nothing. Check the\nconfiguration with the feature flags editor."],[1597,"Every key of general.features/feedback, and which ones a consumer actually checks."],[1592,"Every key of the app's general configuration, and which ones actually gate behavior."],[1626,"Every key of the app's general configuration, and which ones actually gate behavior."],[1565,"Every key of the app's general.features/feedback configuration, which ones actually gate behavior, and the live admin editor for testing them."],[397,"Every mode a Sinequa application signs a user in with — credentials, SSO, OAuth, SAML, bearer — funnels\nthrough the same handful of pieces: a guard that protects routes, an interceptor that carries the session on\nthe `HttpClient` channel, and four views `AuthPageComponent` switches between."],[1768,"Every mutation method (`bookmark()`, `createAlert()`, `updateLanguage()`, …) both patches the store and\npersists the change to the backend API in the same call — there is no separate \"save\" step, and a signal read\nanywhere in the app reflects the change immediately."],[1770,"Every mutator that logs activity also accepts an optional `auditEvents` parameter, forwarded to the audit\ninterceptor."],[1439,"Every one of these methods `postMessage`s the iframe registered through `setIframe()` — `<preview-content>`\ndoes that registration for you once its own iframe mounts. Called before any iframe is registered (or while\nthe previous document's iframe is still tearing down), the message has nowhere to go and is silently dropped;\nthere is no queueing or replay."],[1059,"Every store, service and component in this library reaches the Sinequa backend through **one client**,\nresolved from the `ATOMIC_CLIENT` injection token. `provideAtomicClient()` is how an application gives that\ntoken its own client instead of the default one."],[26,"Every store, service and component reaches the backend through one client. Registering it and bootstrapping\nthe application are two providers in `app.config.ts`."],[2900,"Everything in one object"],[1290,"Everything involved in showing a document once it has been selected: the preview surface itself (an iframe, or\na Markdown fallback), the action bar above it (find, zoom, pages, highlights, converter choice), a\nprojectable metadata header, and the small directives that turn a click or a keypress into a selection."],[2229,"Exclusive selection within a native-name group."],[662,"Expected — `(rangeSelected)` only reports the drag; it changes nothing on its own. See \"How it works\" above:\nkeep a stack of ranges in the host and re-fetch on push/pop."],[683,"Expected — `<Heatmap>` is capped at 20×20 by default and is not meant to grow into the thousands: the DOM node\ncount is what buys its accessibility (real buttons, screen-reader support, text selection), and that stops\nscaling long before a canvas would. Reach for\n`<AggregationHeatmap>` instead — same inputs, same output payloads, an import\nchange — and accept the accessibility trade-off it documents."],[2308,"Expected — `SearchInput` has no `search` output and no send button by design: submission is driven by the\nsurrounding form (native `submit`, a button, or `(keydown.enter)` on the input), consistent with it being \"just\nanother field\" in a larger form. A `(search)` written on `<SearchInput>` would only listen to the browser's native\n`search` event (an `Event`, not text): do not use it. Reach for `SearchBar` when a self-contained field with its own submit is\nwanted."],[840,"Expected — a date facet has no \"resolved but empty\" state: it is either missing (always hidden) or present\n(always visible), because its custom range stays usable with no bucket at all. `hideWhenEmpty` only ever\naffects `<aggregation-list>`/`<aggregation-tree>`."],[1008,"Expected — mobile always uses the bottom Sheet, checked first and independently of `enrichedThreshold`. That\ninput only arbitrates between the desktop Popover and Dialog."],[726,"Expected in a narrow or short container: words that find no free space during placement are dropped, not\noverlapped. The dropped count renders as a small note in the corner (`N not shown`) — if the omission matters,\neither lower `limit`, enlarge the container, or use `<TagCloud>`, which never drops\nanything since it only wraps."],[2831,"Expected on the very first paint of a popover that has never opened before: the element starts\n`visibility: hidden` until the first `computePosition` resolves, specifically to avoid a flash at an\nunpositioned spot. If you still see a visible flash, check that nothing overrides that initial visibility with\na `class` input."],[77,"Expected once the record it points to is genuinely gone from both the original query and the app's default\nquery — not a bug in the list itself. The warning is the fallback path's own signal that neither search found\nthe document, distinct from a bookmark that simply has not loaded yet."],[2439,"Expected the second way, not the first: `pulse`'s halo animates nothing under `prefers-reduced-motion` — a\nblinking indicator is precisely what such a user asked to be spared (WCAG 2.3.3). If you instead reach for\n`class=\"animate-pulse\"` for a softer, no-halo variation, pair it with `motion-reduce:animate-none` yourself;\nand do not stack the two — `animate-pulse` fades the whole element, halo included, cancelling `pulse` out."],[372,"Expected while either password field is still empty: `required` already covers that case, and showing both\r\nmessages at once helps nobody. The mismatch message appears once both fields have content."],[2723,"Expected, and it depends on which host you used. On a real `<dialog>` tag, `show()` opens **non-modally** — no\nbackdrop, no native `Escape` handling, by browser design; only `showModal()`/`openModal()` get those. On a\n`[dialog]` **attribute** host, there is no such distinction: the component cannot tell `show()` from\n`showModal()` there, so `show()` still gets the manual backdrop and the manual `document:keydown.escape`\nlistener."],[797,"Expected, and not a missing feature — `<aggregation-date>` has no `hideWhenEmpty` input at all. A date facet\nhas no \"resolved but empty\" state to gate behind one: its custom range stays usable with zero buckets, so it\nis either missing (always hidden) or present (always visible). See\nAggregation's missing-vs-empty rules."],[841,"Expected, and the same contract as the list. The app-wide `features.quickFilter` flag is a **node-label**\nshortcut only — clicking the label applies in one gesture, but the checkbox, the row and Space/Enter always\njust select and reveal the **Apply** button. Set `[applyOnSelect]=\"true\"` on the instance to make every\ngesture apply immediately, independently of the app-wide flag."],[1513,"Expected: `Tabs`/`TabList`/`Tab` (`@sinequa/galactik`) delegate ARIA roles, keyboard navigation and roving\n`tabindex` to `@angular/aria/tabs` via `hostDirectives` — but the \"more\" button is deliberately never\nregistered as a `Tab`, so it does not participate in arrow-key navigation between tabs. It is still reachable:\nit is the last child of `TabList` (inside the same pill, not floating beside it) and opens its menu on click,\nEnter or Space."],[1623,"Expected: a bare-key shortcut is ignored while focus is in a text field, `contenteditable`, a `<select>` or an\nARIA text role — the keystroke belongs to the field. Add a modifier other than Shift if the shortcut needs to\nfire while typing."],[2390,"Expected: per the `field-sizing` spec, `rows`/`cols` have no effect once `field-sizing: content` applies. Use\n`minRows`/`maxRows` to bound the height instead — they compile to `min-height`/`max-height`, the only sizing\n`field-sizing` honours. Keep writing `rows` anyway: it is what the unsupported-engine (Firefox) fallback uses."],[1399,"Expected: the Markdown branch renders the raw content through the `markdown` pipe directly into a `<div>`, not\ninto `preview.js`'s instrumented iframe — so nothing there can `postMessage` a search or a highlight toggle.\nOnly the converter dropdown and a locally-reimplemented zoom (CSS `zoom`, not the iframe's transform-based one)\nsurvive on that branch."],[2884,"Expected. `dismissible` only neutralizes the scrim click — `Escape` is native `<dialog>` behavior, and the\ncomponent does not fight it. Suppressing `Escape` would trap a keyboard user inside the panel, which is worse\nthan the dismissal you were trying to prevent."],[1257,"Expected. When the session lapses, the client signs in again by itself — a redirect to the identity provider, which\nreloads the page — so there is nothing to ask the user to do. The toast appears when signing in again is not\npossible without them: a credentials form, an OIDC session whose identity provider session has also ended."],[1556,"Exporting `THEMES` from its own file is worth doing as soon as a theme carries more than a couple of colors —\na full color set is a large literal, and keeping it out of `app.config.ts` keeps the bootstrap file readable."],[859,"Exports"],[426,"Extending the form"],[1209,"Extends Angular's own `DatePipe`, passing `TranslocoService`'s current language as the `locale` argument on\nevery transform — the format string (`'mediumDate'`, `'short'`, …) is Angular's own, only the locale follows\nthe interface language automatically instead of the app's static `LOCALE_ID`."],[2974,"External link"],[33,"Facet types, controlled mode, custom item templates, and every input and pitfall in depth."],[96,"Favorites are keyed by the query text, and only recent searches can be starred. A search that was deleted from the\nhistory loses its favorite; running it again creates a new, un-starred recent search."],[1564,"Feature flags"],[1594,"Feature flags, keyboard shortcuts and user settings/profile — looked up, not learned."],[571,"Feedback button"],[798,"Feeding `selectionChange`'s payload straight back into `[selection]` is safe: seeding the form from the\n`[selection]` input is guarded internally against re-triggering a live emission. If you see a loop, check that\n`selection` is a **stable value** between renders (built in a `computed()`/signal, not an inline object\nliteral) — the same rule as `<Aggregation>`'s own `[aggregation]` input, see\nits pitfall."],[1428,"Fetch a document's preview data, drive its zoom and pagination, and toggle its highlights — the service every preview component delegates to."],[1454,"Fetch surrounding-context text chunks for a document's highlight locations, from the Sinequa backend."],[1297,"Fetch surrounding-context text chunks for a set of highlight locations."],[1441,"Fetch surrounding-context text chunks for a set of highlight locations."],[1296,"Fetch, close, zoom and paginate — the service every preview component delegates to."],[904,"Filter button"],[670,"Filtering from an axis label"],[972,"Filtering results"],[925,"Filters bar"],[980,"Filters beyond the bar's visible count — popover, Dialog, or a mobile Sheet."],[950,"Filters panel"],[2849,"Filters sliding in from the right, a navigation panel from the left, a mobile action tray from the bottom —\n`Sheet` is that edge-anchored panel. It is built on a native `<dialog>` opened with `showModal()`, exactly as\nDialog is: a sheet **is** a modal dialog, only its geometry differs, so both share the same\n`DIALOG_REF`/`MODAL_LABEL` tokens and the same `DialogEvent` close events."],[2063,"Finding text has to read the frame, so it only works when the converted copy is served from the **same origin** as\nthe page. Otherwise the box is disabled, and says why in its tooltip."],[218,"Fits the popup to the screen: its height is capped by the room left on the side it opens (the list scrolls inside). In `inline` mode it is then placed by Floating UI instead of staying in the flow."],[3012,"Fixed in the current component, but worth knowing why it happened: `<aside>` used to carry an\nalways-active `translateX(0)`. Per the CSS Transforms spec, **any** transform value other than `none` —\nincluding one that moves nothing — establishes a new containing block for `position: fixed`/`absolute`\ndescendants. A `Menu`/`Popover`/`Dialog` projected into `sidebarContent`/`sidebarFooter` is exactly such a\ndescendant, and floating-ui still measures the *real* viewport for its placement decisions — so the\ncomputed placement gets applied against the wrong containing block, commonly looking like it \"flipped\" to\nthe wrong side no matter which `placement` was requested. If you see this with a custom fork or an older\nversion, check that the transform resolves to the literal keyword `none` whenever no slide is in progress."],[1755,"Fixed in the version that creates the shared profile resource with the service's injector. Before it, the\nresource was created in the form — inside the dialog — and destroyed with it, while the service kept handing out\nthat dead resource. If you call `getUserProfile()` yourself, create nothing around it: it already survives the\ncomponent that asked for it."],[1710,"Flip it, or delete it to get the default back."],[2742,"Floating panel"],[860,"Folding"],[2362,"For a choice among known options, with suggestions, use `Autocomplete` instead: `TagInput`\nnever proposes anything and accepts any text."],[1740,"For a few seconds after a save. The field also takes galactik's `success` look."],[1616,"For a shortcut with no control behind it — a help dialog, a diagnostics panel."],[711,"For a two-dimensional distribution instead of a ranked one-dimensional list."],[1667,"For example Product Owner."],[1675,"For example Sinequa."],[2960,"For floating content the user must read or interact with."],[2726,"For state that should survive a close/reopen cycle, lift it above the dialog (a parent component field, a\nservice) rather than holding it in a component that only exists while the dialog is open."],[374,"Forgot Password"],[2223,"Form"],[2224,"Form controls — Checkbox, Radio, Switch, Input, Textarea, Search fields, Select and Autocomplete — and how they compose with Angular Signal Forms."],[1211,"Formats with `Intl.NumberFormat` in the language `TranslocoService` holds. Angular's `number` pipe follows `LOCALE_ID`, which an\napplication fixes once, so it cannot follow a language change; this one reads the language as a signal and stays pure while still\nupdating the text when the user switches language. `null` and `undefined` are written as `0`. The result is a string: pass it to a\ntranslation (`{ count: n | localizedNumber }`) after choosing the singular or plural key from the number itself."],[52,"Four steps take you from an empty Angular 22 workspace to a form built entirely from `@sinequa/galactik`\ncomponents, styled by its design tokens."],[1633,"Free-form properties: `customData`"],[2185,"Free-text creation"],[189,"From the field, Shift+Tab goes up to the tabs (left and right arrows change tab, Tab goes down into the list), Shift+Tab again comes back to the field and Escape closes the popup. The arrows in either list put the text of the active row in the field."],[812,"Full control over the data and the selection"],[1659,"Full name"],[2492,"Galactik has no translation layer: the sentence and the key's name are yours to provide. `description` must\ncontain `shortcut` as is for the key to be set apart as a keycap inside it. A key that only exists on some\nkeyboards is the caller's to add — a MacBook has no dedicated `Delete` (it is `fn+⌫`, and `⌫` alone emits\n`Backspace`), so declare both there. `isApplePlatform()` is exported for that."],[2291,"Galactik icons render with `display: contents`, so the `<svg>` itself is the flex item — inside the pill's tight\nlayout it collapses without an explicit size. Add `shrink-0` to a bare projected icon; icons already wrapped in\na `<Button>` are unaffected."],[15,"Getting started"],[45,"Getting started"],[1339,"Give `actions` a list of `OverflowAction` (an `id`, an already translated `label` and an icon component). They follow the\nbuilt-in buttons and move into the menu once the row is full. `selected` emits the `id` of the one that was chosen, from\nits button or from the menu."],[1073,"Give a route or component subtree its own client, plus the stores and services it needs."],[1091,"Give a route or component subtree its own Sinequa client plus a self-contained copy of the library's stores and services, so two backends never leak into each other."],[1050,"Give an application its own Sinequa client — its own configuration, session and event subscribers — instead of the default one backing the free functions."],[2779,"Give another panel the Menu's look"],[1168,"Give the application its own Sinequa client instead of the default one."],[2615,"Give the group an `autoSaveId` and the layout is remembered in `localStorage`, under the key\n`resizable-panel:<autoSaveId>` — restored on the next visit, but only if the group still has the same number\nof panels; otherwise the panels' own `defaultSize`s are the better answer."],[194,"Give the popup your own content with an `<ng-template searchBoxPopup>`, and your own source with `suggestionsProvider`.\nThe template replaces the tabs and their lists; the card, its placement and its opening