ion, the principal and\nthe user settings — **in parallel**: none depends on another's answer, only on the session, so they take one\nround trip rather than three. It then applies them to `AppStore`, `PrincipalStore` and `UserSettingsStore` in\nthat order, resetting `QueryParamsStore` between the principal and the settings. A failed read is handled\nexactly as before: the configuration and the principal stop the start-up, the settings fall back to their\ndefaults."],[2621,"One handle sits between every two panels, in document order — the group pairs the handle at index *i* with\nthe panels at index *i* and *i+1*. A handle placed elsewhere in the projected content resizes nothing."],[2331,"One limit: a projected `[selectTrigger]` gets no automatic name — put an `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby` on it."],[978,"One popover button per authorized facet, with overflow handled by More."],[1615,"One stack per combination: the **last** registration wins, and the previous one comes back once it\nunregisters — modeling what a panel opening over a page should do to the shortcuts underneath it."],[2729,"Only `aria-labelledby` is wired automatically, through the `MODAL_LABEL` token shared between `DialogTitle` and\n`DialogContent`. There is no equivalent auto-wiring for `DialogDescription` into `aria-describedby`."],[1083,"Only HTTP statuses `400`, `403`, `500` and `503` raise a `notify.error(…)` toast; an impersonation rejected by the\nserver (`401` with `errorCode: 6`) gets its own explicit message. Every other failure is silent: `404`, `429`, `502`,\n`504`, and any failure without an HTTP response (network error, timeout), which the client does not report as a\n`requestFailed` event. A plain `401` raises nothing either — it is handled by the authentication path, not shown to\nthe user; `provideSessionExpiry()` is the opt-in that tells the user their session ended.\nTwo more sources of noise are silenced on top of that: a `400` on `api/v2/user-profile` (the expected \"not creat