ender in the page's own DOM, not in a shadow root, and through the application's injector: they share its\nTransloco configuration, its `@sinequa/atomic` setup and its `WorkspacesStore` with the rest of the page."],[758,"The emitted `AggregationSelection` is `{ kind: \"option\", option }` for a preset — the item's real filter\n`value`, never its `display`, so a round-trip survives across days for presets computed relative to today —\nor `{ kind: \"range\", from, to }` for a custom range."],[2332,"The empty state of `value` must be `null`, never `undefined` — setting it to `undefined` removes the property\nfrom the field entirely, which Signal Forms reports as an orphan field (`NG01902`) rather than a valid empty\nvalue. Type the field as `string | null` (or your option type `| null`), initial `null`, and never write\n`undefined` to it yourself."],[1137,"The endpoint answers with a `StartupData`: `app`, `principal` and `userSettings`, each one a `StartupPart` — `{ \"ok\": true, \"value\": … }` when the BFF read it, `{ \"ok\": false, \"status\": … }`\nwhen it could not. Any other key — mint-dev-server's BFF also sends `userProfile` — is ignored: the profile is\nread when the account settings panel opens, as without the provider. Here the settings call failed on the\nserver:"],[612,"The equivalent for the Sinequa client's own requests, on a different channel."],[1737,"The error"],[152,"The explicitly-named counterpart — a starred toggle and a save dialog."],[969,"The facets of the \"All\" view, usable on their own."],[1361,"The field submits to `SelectionStore.queryText`: the preview reloads with the text highlighted in the document.\nIts results panel — **Snippet** (where the text matches), **Extracts**, **Entities**, then Labels and Similar\ndocuments when the document has them — opens under the field as soon as it takes the focus, and closes on"],[951,"The filters column of a search page in one piece — facets with a search field, and the user's quick filters."],[1351,"The find field"],[1337,"The first `maxInline` places of the row (3 by default) are filled in that order and the rest goes into the \"…\" menu:\nwith the three built-in buttons, the menu only appears once the host adds an action. Content projected into the\ncomponent is never counted: it follows the buttons in the row, as it is."],[1601,"The five preview highlight categories, and how to override their colors."],[112,"The floating variant"],[149,"the footer, to the left of \"See all\", reads \"↑ ↓ to navigate\" and \"Enter to open\", the keys drawn as keycaps."],[384,"The forgot-password form asks for a username and requests a password-reset email for that account. It comes in\r\ntwo components over one implementation: `ForgotPasswordFormComponent` (`<forgot-password-form>`) is the form alone —\r\nno logo, no card — and embeds anywhere; `ForgotPasswordComponent` (`<forgot-password>`) adds the logo and a card, and\r\nis the screen behind the \"forgot password\" link of Sign In, reached through\r\n`AuthPageComponent` on `/login?mode=forgotpassword`."],[569,"The form does not contain its submit button. Put it anywhere and give it `[attr.form]=\"form.formId\"` (with\n`#form` on `<alert-form>`): a button that is not inside the form and has no `form` attribute submits nothing.\nInside the form's own markup, `ButtonComponent` does not set `type` for you — a button left untyped in a\n`<form>` submits it, so give every other button an explicit `type=\"button\"`."],[1649,"The form model is a `linkedSignal`: a successful save, a deletion or a profile reload re-seeds every field from\nserver state, which is what discards a cancelled draft with no manual DOM restore."],[558,"The form renders no Cancel or Confirm of its own: they belong to the container. It emits `saved` once the save has\nsucceeded, and `executed` once the user has run the watched search (the query parameters then hold it)."],[366,"The form sits in the dialog body; Cancel and Confirm are the `DialogFooter`'s. To build your own dialog, render\r\n`<change-password-form #form [showActions]=\"false\" />` and bind Confirm to `form.canSubmit()` / `form.changePassword()`."],[385,"The form sits in the dialog body; Cancel and Send are the `DialogFooter`'s."],[1760,"The form the Account panel hosts inline when the deployment allows it."],[2842,"The four sides"],[2067,"The frame is from another origin, so the page may not read its text (\"This document cannot be searched from here.\"). Serve\nthe converted copy under the page's own origin, for instance behind a reverse proxy, to enable the search."],[60,"The full imperative call/result API this page's example only introduces."],[793,"The full list (month/year grids, days outside the month…) is in the generated stylesheet, under the\n`date-range-calendar` rule at its end. Layout — sizes, spacing, radii — comes from vanilla-calendar-pro and is\nbest left alone; the dialog sizes itself to the two months."],[158,"The full list, with filter counts and relative dates"],[1291,"The full preview surface — load, render, zoom, page, and fall back to Markdown when needed."],[1371,"The full preview surface this bar is normally nested inside."],[2425,"The generated icon catalog (`CircleCheckIcon`, `BellIcon`, …) is exported from the main `@sinequa/galactik` barrel, like\nevery other component. `@sinequa/ui` exports over a hundred icons under the **same class names** — in a file\nimporting from both libraries, alias the import or take every icon from a single source to avoid silently\npicking the wrong one."],[2613,"The group takes the full size of its parent (`size-full`), so it needs a parent with a height — one in a\nplain `<div>` with no height collapses."],[2173,"The group's `value` model is always a `string[]`, even in single-selection mode — bind an array signal."],[306,"The guard lets `/login` and `/logout` through unconditionally — guarding the login form against \"not\nlogged in\" would redirect it to itself, and guarding `/logout` would