on, extract locations, match locations — and how to override their colors."],[2292,"The inline-form sibling, styled like InputGroup, no send button."],[1143,"The inlined data describes the session the page was rendered for, so the source reads it once and removes it:\nafter a sign-out and a sign-in — possibly as someone else — it throws, and the three parts are read again."],[1172,"The interface language, audit metadata and 401 recovery, on the HttpClient channel."],[2512,"The keyboard path is the action's key on the focused row (`keys`, `Delete` by default): `<ListItem>` sets\n`aria-keyshortcuts` from it whenever it projects a usable `ListItemAction`, and pressing the key calls the\naction's `trigger()` on your behalf — your `(click)` handler on `<ListItemAction>` still fires, unchanged.\nSee Row action and its key. `ListItemExpander` is the exception in this family: it\ndoes render a real `<button>`, reachable by `Tab` in the usual way."],[1650,"The layout is one card per bucket — **Information** for the configured standard fields, **Preferences** for the\nfree-form ones (the card is left out when there are none) — in one or two columns depending on the width of the\ndialog. Each field is a plain text input with its actions inside the box, always visible: edit and delete at rest,\nsave and cancel while editing."],[723,"The layout re-runs whenever the aggregation data, the container size, or web-font readiness changes — the last\none matters because the canvas used to measure each word's ink box needs the real font metrics, not a\nfallback, to place words tightly."],[1254,"The library has no toast layer of its own: it only emits `notify` events, so what a `duration` means belongs to\nyour toast bridge. `0` is \"never closes on its own\" for `sonner-a11y`; `Infinity` is not, because a non-finite delay\nreaches a timer that fires straight away. If your bridge reads `0` differently, set `expiredDuration` to what it\nneeds."],[2644,"The library translates nothing, so a