on, and pieces you lay out yourself — see\nMention workspaces."],[1826,"The message for when correction still finds nothing."],[3002,"The mobile drawer reuses `Sheet` unmodified — focus trap, `Escape`-to-close, focus restoration and the\n`::backdrop` all come from the native `<dialog>` + `showModal()` — sized to the full viewport width (a fixed\n`Sheet` width can otherwise push the in-header trigger off-screen on a narrow phone) and painted with the same\n`--sidebar`/`--sidebar-foreground` tokens as the desktop panel, so a themed app gets a matching drawer with no\nextra work."],[3001,"The mobile drawer starts closed, and its entire content — including a trigger placed inside `sidebarHeader` —\nlives inside it. Below the breakpoint there is nothing on screen to open it from unless the app keeps a\n**second** trigger outside the `<Sidebar>` (its own top bar, typically), passed the panel explicitly since it\ncannot resolve `SIDEBAR_REF` through DI from outside:"],[3015,"The modal panel the mobile drawer reuses unmodified."],[387,"The model is two-way bindable, which is what lets a wizard carry the username from a previous step."],[2250,"The multi-line sibling, sharing the same state model and scheme palette."],[2232,"The multi-line sibling, with content-driven auto-sizing."],[2353,"The multi-select sibling, with an indeterminate state and Signal Forms integration."],[2221,"The mutually-exclusive sibling — grouped by native name attribute rather than a container component."],[2463,"The name passed to `KbdGroup` should be the ARIA form of the combination (`Control+Shift+F`) — which is also\nwhat belongs in `aria-keyshortcuts` on the control the\nshortcut drives — while the visible keys can use the shorter labels a user reads on their own keyboard\n(`Ctrl`, `⌥`). The visual and the announced form must agree."],[2832,"The native auto-invoke behavior for `popovertarget` only applies to `<button>`/`<input type=\"button\">`\nelements. A `<div>` or similar acting as a trigger