o a fresh application\nbootstrap (and a fresh sign-in attempt) starts from scratch."],[2062,"The panel asks the preview web service for the document by id, as a search application does, and shows the converted\ncopy the service points at in a frame. Until the backend hands out the index id for an uploaded document (the listing\ncarries the upload-side id) the service answers an error — the panel then says the document cannot be previewed,\nrather than showing a stand-in."],[2910,"The panel is a `role=\"tooltip\"` element created on demand — inside the closest `<dialog>` or `[popover]` when the host is in one (a modal dialog makes everything outside it `inert`, and a popover closes on a click outside of it: left on `body`, the tooltip could no longer be hovered or clicked), in `body` otherwise — and positioned by\n`injectFloatingPanel` as a manual popover: it renders in the top layer, above a `<dialog>`\nand outside the clipping of any ancestor, with no `z-index`. Nothing listens on the document while the tooltip is\nclosed — the `Escape`, `scroll` and `click` listeners are added when it opens and removed when it closes."],[89,"The panel is a flex child that grows from `0` to `--history-panel-width` (15.625rem by default) when `open` turns\ntrue, so beside a sidebar it **pushes** the page content instead of covering it. Closed, it is `inert` and\n`aria-hidden`. Under the mobile breakpoint it becomes a `Sheet` sliding from the left. `Escape` and the close\nbutton write `open` back."],[128,"The panel is exported on its own (`AddToCollectionPanelComponent`, outputs `done`, `changed`,\n`closeRequested`) for a host that wants it somewhere else, in a sheet for example."],[958,"The panel is the content only. It fills the height it is given and scrolls inside; whether it is a column next to the results,\nan overlay or a sheet, and the card around it, belong to the page."],[95,"The panel pushes its siblings only when it is a child of a flex row next to them: its width animates, it does not\nposition itself. Put it in the same flex container as the sidebar and the content."],[1989,"The parts the shell is made of, to lay out yourself."],[2087,"The picker and the mention list as `<lexiq-workspace-picker>` and `<lexiq-workspace-mention-list>`."],[2081,"The picker does the work itself (`saveDocuments`, or `moveDocuments` from the store) and resolves once the check mark has\nbeen seen, with `{ type: \"dialog-confirm\", workspace }`. When moving, the workspace the documents come from is left out\nof the list. A new workspace needs a name that no other workspace has, whatever its case — the same name twice cannot\nbe told apart in a list."],[2084,"The picker is for *writing*: a workspace shared read-only stays out of it. It stays in the mention list, which only reads."],[2052,"The picker that puts documents into a workspace, or moves them."],[331,"The pieces"],[1167,"The pieces every application wires in once, regardless of which search features it uses: the client\nconnecting to the backend, the bootstrap sequence that signs the user in, and the interceptors, pipes,\nservices and utilities that cut across every feature rather than belonging to one."],[970,"The pill version of the user's quick filters."],[1392,"The pinned panel is declared by this component, which owns its state, and shown by `<preview-find-panel>` wherever the\nhost puts it: a host that switches `findPanel` between `\"popover\"` and `\"pinned\"` (an expanded view) never moves or\nreloads the iframe. Without a `<preview-find-panel>` in the host's template, nothing shows in `\"pinned\"` mode but the\ntoggle. Below 900px of viewport the card is laid over the document rather than beside it. Escape puts the\npanel away first, and only the next one reaches the host."],[2921,"The placeholder disappears as soon as the field holds a value, whatever `isClipped()` says: add `!!text()` to the\ncondition, as above. The measure is taken when the field is rendered, then again whenever its size or its\n`placeholder` changes and once the fonts are loaded. It uses the canvas text metrics, with the letter spacing and the\n`uppercase` text transform of the field, against its width minus its horizontal padding (1 px of slack). Nothing is\nmeasured on the server, where `isClipped()` stays `false`. The placeholder is not always the accessible name of the\nfield: give it its own (`aria-label`), the tooltip being a pointer help."],[727,"The placement measures text with the real web font once `document.fonts.ready` resolves — before that, the\nfirst layout pass may use fallback metrics. This resolves itself automatically and re-lays out; it is not a\nbug to guard against in host code."],[1318,"The plain-click/Enter counterpart, for selecting rather than opening externally."],[999,"The popover can be resized in height, as a filter button's one: a handle on its top edge (which keeps the bottom edge\nwhere it is) and one on its bottom edge (hidden when there is no room under the popover). The handles take the mouse, a\nfinger and the keyboard: they are focusable separators, Up and Down move them by 16px, Home goes to the smallest height and\nEnd to the largest. The list of facets fills the height it is given and scrolls. From the first resize the popover stays\nwhere it is while it is open, instead of flipping or shifting under the pointer; closing it, or scrolling the page, lets\nFloating UI place it again, and the height the user chose is kept. The Dialog and the mobile Sheet are not resizable."],[919,"The popover can be resized in height, from a handle on its top edge (which keeps the bottom edge where it is) and one on its\nbottom edge (hidden when there is no room under the popover). The handles take the mouse, a finger and the keyboard: they are\nfocusable separators, and Up and Down move them by 16px, Home goes to the smallest height and End to the largest. The facet fills\nthe height it is given and its list scrolls. From the first resize the popover stays where it is while it is open, instead of\nflipping or shifting under the pointer; closing it, or scrolling the page, lets Floating UI place it again, and the height the\nuser chose is kept."],[916,"The popover is a native `[popover]` element (top layer): it can never be clipped by an ancestor's\n`overflow`/`z-index`, and only the viewport itself bounds its size. Its inner `<Aggregation>` is capped to the\nactual available space between the trigger and the viewport edge:"],[166,"The popover reads whether the current search is already saved from `UserSettingsStore.getSavedSearch(queryText)`\n— there is no separate \"saved\" input to keep in sync yourself."],[918,"The popover shows the facet alone, `headless`: no icon, no title and no collapse chevron, since the button already\nsays which facet it is. Under the search field a bar holds a **Clear all** button and, while a choice is pending, **Apply** — without an icon.\nRight above the items, a list or tree facet has a **Select all** row: its checkbox is labelled, and the label carries the\nnumber of selected items (\"Select all (3)\", \"Deselect all (12)\" once everything is checked; a live text gives the count to\nscreen readers). The checkbox is mixed while only some items are selected, applied ones included. **Clear all** is disabled\nwhile nothing is selected or applied; it empties the selection and keeps the popover open so another choice can be made.\nOnly **Apply** closes the popover. A date facet has no search field, so it gets the same bar at its top."],[253,"The popup opened or closed."],[185,"The popup opens when the field gets the focus and goes back to the **Suggestions** tab each time it opens."],[2959,"The positioning helper the tooltip is placed with."],[2805,"The positioning primitive Menu is built on — reach for it directly for content that isn't a list of actions."],[2767,"The positioning primitive Menu is built on, for any floating content that isn't a list of actions."],[448,"The post-logout confirm