g follows the date the client was last told. A server that **extends** active sessions without sending the\nrenewed token (no `sinequa-jwt-refresh`) lets that date run out while the session carries on, and the user is warned\nfor nothing. The client cannot tell the two apart. The backends observed so far do not behave this way: one ends the\nsession a fixed time after sign-in whatever the user does, the other sends the renewed token on every response."],[555,"The whole form is one Signal Forms field tree (`[formRoot]`), and the Confirm button **is** the form's\n`submit` — there is no separate click handler that reads the model and calls a service. The seven weekday\nchips bind to plain booleans, one native checkbox each; `Alert.Days` (the bitfield the server actually stores)\nonly exists at the edges, folded by `flagsFromWeekdays()`/unfolded by `weekdaysFromFlags()`. Two shortcuts,\n\"Weekdays\" and \"Every day\", check them in one click, and an `Immediate` alert does not show them at all."],[1988,"The whole view in one component."],[1277,"The worker function's body is extracted by calling `.toString()` on it and stripping the outer `function(){ }`\nwrapper — it never actually closes over the surrounding scope, so any reference to a variable, import, or\n`this` from outside the function is simply undefined inside the worker. Write the worker function as fully\nself-contained, using only what a Web Worker's global scope (`self`, `postMessage`) provides."],[2100,"The workspace is not in the store yet. Load the workspaces first (`WorkspacesStore.ensureLoaded()`), or open the\ndialog from a view that has."],[1845,"The zero-match message — and where pagination for a result list actually lives now."],[1363,"The zoom buttons act on the iframe through `PreviewService`, and disable themselves at the bounds the iframe\nannounces. The page navigation shows only while the document has more than one page, follows the page being read\nas the user scrolls, and takes the first and 