eys` keeps out\npeople who already have access, `closeOnPick` closes the list and clears the text after a pick — a chat's\nmention box — and an element marked `autocompleteSuffix` is projected inside the field, after the text."],[875,"When the chips wrap onto more than `maxLines` lines (2 by default), the list is folded to that height: the rest sits behind a\nfade, and a **Show more** button appears at the bottom right of the zone while the pointer is on it or the focus is in it (always\non a screen with no hover). It unfolds the list with a short height animation, and the same button says **Show less**. The chips in\nthe folded part are `inert`, so a remove button nobody can see is not a tab stop. `maxLines=\"0\"` never folds."],[1805,"When the engine corrects a misspelled query, three different things could actually have happened to the\nsearch: the corrected term fully replaced the original, both spellings were searched together, or nothing was\nsearched yet and the engine only proposes a correction. `<did-you-mean>` reads which one from the result and\nrenders the matching message, with links to switch spellings."],[2347,"When the label cannot be projected, name the inner `<input role=\"switch\">` with one of the two inputs below.\nDo not wrap the switch in a `<label>`: it already renders its own, and nested labels are invalid."],[2179,"When to use it"],[1005,"When you use `<more>` alone, give it a bounded height in a flex column (`flex h-[60vh] flex-col`): the facet's own list is\nthen the one scroller. In a plain `max-h` + `overflow-y-auto` wrapper it still works, the wrapper scrolling instead."],[802,"Where a date facet like this one is typically opened from — one popover per filter."],[570,"Where a failed request's own error notifications come from."],[881,"Where a selection actually gets made, before it reaches the applied-filters\nstore."],[1759,"Where general.features.userProfile and allowChangePassword are configured."],[1503,"Where the counts and the persisted-filters behavior come from"],[948,"Where the filters beyond filtersCount go, and how it adapts to mobile."],[1642,"Where the focus lands"],[1796,"Where the loaded PreviewData this component reads conversions from comes from."],[1037,"Where the popover goes."],[1825,"Where the Result this component reads from comes from."],[1943,"Where the Result this component reads sortingChoices from comes from."],[2119,"Where the upload button lives."],[923,"Where these buttons are rendered from, and how overflow is handled."],[314,"Where this guard fits among the interceptor, sign-in and logout."],[1426,"Where this header typically sits, above the iframe or Markdown fallback."],[1009,"Where this overflow button is normally mounted from."],[1263,"Where to register it again when a second backend has its own client."],[533,"Whether labels are available at all — and which article fields hold the public/private lists — comes from the\nSinequa server's **labels web service** configuration, read through `LabelService.getLabelsConfig()`. An app\nwith no labels web service configured has no label fields to show; `EditLabels` renders nothing in that case\nrather than an empty dialog."],[583,"Which entries appear comes from `general.feedback` in the application configuration — see\nFeature flags. Every switch defaults to on, and when all six are off the\nbutton is not rendered at all."],[1807,"Which message renders depends entirely on the resolved `action` — a computed the component derives from the\nresult, never set directly:"],[1883,"Which of the query's terms this particular document doesn't contain, struck through, each a link to re-run the search requiring all of them."],[1846,"Which query terms this particular document doesn't contain, each a link to search for them all."],[2114,"While a job is moving, the service matches the server's documents listing to the tracked files by job and file name\n(the server names a document `/DocUpload/DocUpload/|<containerId>/<fileName>`, not `<jobId>/<fileName>`), and a file\ntakes the server's id as soon as the listing shows it — that is the id a delete needs. `sent_for_indexing` counts as\n`indexing`, and a file completes when its job does. The server only reports indexing per job (indexed files out of\ntotal), so the tracker's uploading and indexing bars show the overall progress of the phase (`UploadTrackerStore.progress()`),\nand files being indexed show animated dots rather than the job's percentage. The workspace detail only lists documents\nthat are indexed or being indexed: transfers and failures stay in the tracker."],[1744,"While the row is edited. For an array: *Edit the JSON array · Escape to cancel* (Enter adds a line)."],[488,"While the user still has bookmarks, a **Bookmarks** tab sits above the list. A click on a bookmark opens its document in\nthe same preview as a document of a collection: `<preview-content>` on the right of the list, in a resizable panel,\nreplacing the list when the component is narrow. A bookmark only keeps what the old list showed (id, label, source,\nauthor), so the preview looks the document up by its id, with the current query of the application, not the one the\nbookmark was made from. Bookmarks can also be ticked and moved to a collection the same way, which is how old\nbookmarks are migrated; the tab disappears with the last bookmark. A moved document is loaded again by the\ncollection's detail, with the default query of the application."],[1907,"Who runs the search"],[459,"Why /logout renders this view instead of the sign-in form, end to end."],[1165,"Wiring the client, bootstrap, and cross-cutting interceptors, pipes, services and utilities into a host application."],[2955,"With `autoHide` off the tooltip closes the moment the pointer leaves the host, so it cannot be hovered.\nLeave `autoHide` on (the default): a 100 ms grace lets the pointer cross the gap."],[1497,"With a session already in place (every application started with `bootstrapApp()`), the component marks the\napplication ready at once, restores the `returnUrl` query parameters into `QueryParamsStore` and navigates to it;\nwithout a `returnUrl` it goes to `/`. In earlier versions it never got ready in such an application and ended on\n`/error` after five seconds."],[2329,"With neither `fieldLabel` nor `aria-label`, the default trigger has no accessible name beyond its own text — a\nscreen reader says “Apple”, with no hint of what is being chosen. Give every select one of the two. The default\ntrigger is then named `aria-labelledby` the label first and itself second (“Fruit, Apple”), so the current value\nstays part of the announcement; a native `<label for>` would not do that, since it replaces a button's content in\nthe name. The popup's list carries the same name."],[964,"with none saved, the empty state says how to make one."],[90,"With nothing to list, each tab shows the usual empty state of the list features — a pastel icon tile (blue history icon under All, yellow star under Favorites), a short title and one hint line."],[2270,"With suggestions"],[2296,"With suggestions"],[1138,"With that answer, `AppStore` and `PrincipalStore` take their value without a request, and `GET\napi/v1/user-settings` is sent from the browser: every part the BFF could not read — or that its answer lacks —\nis fetched the usual way, all of them in parallel, and a failure of that read is handled as before. Only the\nbrowser's own reads can fail the start-up: the `status` or `error` a part reports is never treated as a\nfailure."],[1732,"Without `privateCustomData`, the form behaves as before: no Private card."],[708,"Without `uniformRepartition`, the globally largest items win `limit` regardless of source — one aggregation\nwith many distinct values can crowd out the others entirely."],[1307,"Without a `label` the component is decoration (`aria-hidden=\"true\"`): use it inside a control that already says it is\nbusy, as the Load more button does with `aria-busy`. With a `label` it is a polite live region (`role=\"status\"`) that\nsays it to a screen reader and shows nothing but the dots."],[2079,"Without an injector, `call()` needs `provideCallable()` from `@sinequa/galactik` in the providers."],[2095,"Without an injector, `call()` needs `provideCallable()` from `@sinequa/galactik` in the providers. The workspace has\nto be known to `WorkspacesStore` — loaded by a list, a detail or `ensureLoaded()` — because the dialog reads it from there."],[1135,"Without it, a signed-in start-up costs three requests sent together — `GET api/v1/app`,\n`GET api/v1/principal`, `GET api/v1/user-settings`. Behind a backend-for-frontend (BFF) that makes those calls\nitself, server-side, and answers them all at once — mint-dev-server's BFF answers `GET /bff/bootstrap` —\n`provideStartupAggregation()` replaces all three with a single request. Nothing else changes in the\napplication: the stores are filled exactly as before."],[2285,"Without suggestions, `SearchBar` is a native search field. To show suggestions under it, add the static `suggestions`\nattribute and import `SearchBarSuggestionsComponent` instead: the inner `<input>` then carries `ngCombobox` and is announced\nas a combobox, which it is once a popup is attached. The popup is an `ng-template` bound to the combobox exposed by\n`combobox()`, exactly as for `SearchInput`; the send button still submits the free-text\nquery. The attribute is a choice made once, when the bar is created."],[2302,"Without suggestions, `SearchInput` is a native search field. To show a list of suggestions under it, add the static\n`suggestions` attribute and import `SearchInputSuggestionsComponent` instead: its inner `<input>` then carries\n`ngCombobox`, so assistive technology announces a combobox only when there is a popup to go with it. The popup is yours:\nan `ng-template` bound to the combobox the component exposes through `combobox()`."],[917,"Without this, `flip()`/`shift()` alone only reposition the popover — they never shrink it — so a facet with\nmany values could overflow past the viewport in the gap between the trigger and the screen edge."],[712,"Word Cloud"],[2120,"WorkspacesShell"],[2466,"Write the keys inside a real `<kbd>` element (the role comes from the tag; the directive only styles it), put\nthe accessible name on `KbdGroup`, and mark every key and separator inside it `aria-hidden=\"true\"` — see the\ncombination example above. Without that split, a screen reader reads \"Control\", \"plus\", \"Shift\" as three\nseparate items instead of one shortcut."],[1922,"You checked `records.length` (or `rowCount`) without checking `$error` first — both a genuine zero-match and a\nfailed request (a 500 on a bad filter, most often) arrive as an empty `records` array. Check `failure()`\n(or `result().$error`) before drawing any conclusion from an empty result."],[2721,"You injected `DialogComponent` directly from a sub-component rendered inside the dialog — a custom footer\nbutton, a custom header action. `DialogComponent` renders the very content that would be importing it, so\nthat is a circular dependency, not a plain DI mistake."],[23,"You need a Sinequa server reachable from the browser, with at least one query web service configured. Nothing\nhere works against a mock — the client, the guard and the query service all make real HTTP requests."],[181,"Your own popup and your own suggestions"],[1352,"Zoom and pages"]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":49,"2":50,"3":51,"4":52,"5":53,"6":0,"7":1,"8":2,"9":3,"10":4,"11":5,"12":6,"13":7,"14":8,"15":1808,"16":1809,"17":1810,"18":1811,"19":1812,"20":1813,"21":1814,"22":1815,"23":1816,"24":1817,"25":1818,"26":1819,"27":1820,"28":1821,"29":1822,"30":1823,"31":1824,"32":1825,"33":1826,"34":1827,"35":1828,"36":2112,"37":2113,"38":2114,"39":2115,"40":2116,"41":2117,"42":2118,"43":2119,"44":2120,"45":3022,"46":3023,"47":3024,"48":3025,"49":3026,"50":3027,"51":3028,"52":3029,"53":3030,"54":3031,"55":3032,"56":3033,"57":3034,"58"